{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_28", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(s) for s in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]; targets={\\\"hyp-20261122-002-r10s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261122-002-r11s1\\\",\\\"hyp-20261122-001-r12s0\\\"}; [print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in r.items() if k in (\\\"id\\\",\\\"result\\\",\\\"status\\\",\\\"formal\\\",\\\"fpga\\\",\\\"timing\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\")},indent=2)[:7500]) for r in rows if r.get(\\\"id\\\") in targets]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r10s1\",\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"# MEM completion lane\\n\\nFetch predecodes eligibility for BEQ, BNE, ADD, and ADDI and carries the flag with the issue packet. Packets at the last instruction-aperture word always use the ordinary EX route. Issue keeps the existing interlock for other consumers and captures both regular forwarding selectors and any pending encoded-source matches for eligible consumers. Deferred additions can supply the lane on the next cycle.\\n\\nEX captures the available operand and its ordinary fallback result, along with both forwarded operands for RVFI. EX checks memory alignment and qualifies the producer's write before its consumer enters MEM. MEM uses the registered MEM/WB result for equality or addition and handles a double match directly. ADDI retains its immediate when only its encoded rs2 matches, and RVFI still observes the producer's value for that tag. The EX ALU uses registered operation selects and one right shifter for SRL and SRA. Branch comparisons combine parallel byte comparisons.\\n\\nFetch registers the sequential, prediction, retry, and two recovery addresses. Direct targets use an 18-bit low-word sum and a 12-bit upper adjustment. The qualified prediction register stores 18 bits, while the issue packet and recovery and retry paths preserve the full addressing range.\\n\\nThe older MEM branch has priority on recovery and on the single predictor-training port. The corrected request bypasses the stale FIFO while the read pointer rebases to the current write position. Registered recovery masks younger entries and cancels speculative divider state. MEM holds a missed branch's retirement record through the corrected request, then presents it once through the existing single-channel MEM/WB retirement interface.\\n\\n## Timing changes\\n\\nThe first completion-lane implementation placed at a median of 84.107 MHz. Its limiting paths included the two dependent radix-4 trials in the narrow-divisor recurrence and the EX forwarding path. Narrow divides now use paral\n…[1027 of 4099 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c12a92aae3b3237d]…\nark passed all CRC checks and measured 3,868,036 marker cycles, down 2.81% from 3,979,945.\\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` confirmed that Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 reach 87.120, 96.774, and 96.774 MHz. The 96.774 MHz median clears the 87.793 MHz promotion threshold and scores 250.19 iterations/s, up 15.30% from 216.99. Option 0 was limited by EX forwarding into the data address. Options 1 and 2 were limited by the fetch recovery path into the next direct target. Gowin reported 4,761 logic cells and 1,148 registers, up from 4,224 and 954 for the champion.\\n- Local formal was incomplete. The stock single-channel ALTOPS run generated 53 checks on the final RTL. Liveness, retirement uniqueness, backward PC consistency, and causality passed. The remaining checks had no result within the local budget. The run reported no counterexamples and required zero formal fix attempts.\\n\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r11s1\",\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r12s0\",\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
