{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_52", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,190p' formal/wrapper_si.sv\nsed -n '1,110p' formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-pairedAddiR14s0/checks/cover/logfile.txt | tail -22\nrg -n 'JOBS|TIMEOUT' tools/eval/formal.py\"", "aggregated_output": "// riscv-formal wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. Same shape and\n// memory model as wrapper.sv, but instantiates `core` with only the\n// channel-0 RVFI port set — no `_1` ports. The single-issue path produces\n// only ch0 checks; checks_si.cfg sets `nret 1` so genchecks does not\n// emit any `_ch1` tasks (no PREUNSAT-as-pass tally needed). Selected by\n// the orchestrator when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n`include \"rvfi_macros.vh\"\n\nmodule rvfi_wrapper (\n    input clock,\n    input reset,\n    `RVFI_OUTPUTS\n);\n    // Solver picks any 32-bit instruction each cycle.\n    (* keep *) `rvformal_rand_reg [31:0] imem_data;\n\n    // 8 KiB dmem (2048 words).\n    reg [31:0] dmem [0:2047];\n\n    wire [31:0] imem_addr;\n    wire [31:0] dmem_addr;\n    wire [31:0] dmem_wdata;\n    wire [3:0]  dmem_wen;\n    wire        dmem_ren;\n\n    always @(posedge clock) begin\n        if (dmem_wen[0]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][7:0]   <= dmem_wdata[7:0];\n        if (dmem_wen[1]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][15:8]  <= dmem_wdata[15:8];\n        if (dmem_wen[2]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][23:16] <= dmem_wdata[23:16];\n        if (dmem_wen[3]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][31:24] <= dmem_wdata[31:24];\n    end\n\n    core uut (\n        .clock              (clock),\n        .reset              (reset),\n        .io_imemAddr        (imem_addr),\n        .io_imemData        (imem_data),\n        .io_imemReady       (1'b1),\n        .io_dmemAddr        (dmem_addr),\n        .io_dmemWData       (dmem_wdata),\n        .io_dmemRData       (dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]]),\n        .io_dmemWEn         (dmem_wen),\n        .io_dmemREn         (dmem_ren),\n        .io_dmemReady       (1'b1),\n        // Channel 0 — the only retirement channel. With nret=1 in\n        // checks_si.cfg, every rvfi_* signal here is sized for a single\n        // channel, so the core's `_0` ports connect directly without\n        // slicing. No `_1` ports exist on the core's IO under nret=1.\n        .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid),\n        .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order),\n        .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn),\n\n…[1677 of 4749 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:48d402c7d58eaf49]…\n_0: ##   0:05:17  Writing trace to Verilog testbench: engine_0/trace0_tb.v\nSBY 19:44:15 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:05:17  Writing trace to constraints file: engine_0/trace0.smtc\nSBY 19:44:15 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:05:17  Writing trace to Yosys witness file: engine_0/trace0.yw\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] engine_0: ##   0:05:19  Status: passed\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] engine_0: finished (returncode=0)\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] engine_0: Status returned by engine: pass\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:05:21 (321)\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:01:57 (117)\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) returned pass\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] summary: cover trace: cover/engine_0/trace0.vcd\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] summary:   reached cover statement rvfi_testbench._witness_.check_flatten_checker_inst__cover_cover_stmts_vh_1_51 at cover_stmts.vh:1.23-1.55 step 20\nSBY 19:44:17 [cover] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\n139:                env = {**env, \"JOBS\": eval_jobs()}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
