{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all; sed -n '1,130p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n# Shared EX arithmetic lane\n\n`core_pkg.sv` replaces the separate ADD and SUB selects with `sum_enable`\nand `invert_b`. The existing ID/EX predecode captures both bits. The ALU's\nencoded mode uses the same decode function.\n\n`alu.sv` uses one 12/10/10-bit carry-select lane for ADD, ADDI, SUB, SLT,\nSLTU, SLTI and SLTIU. Each section computes its two local sums in parallel.\nThe carry-one candidate appends a constant one to each operand, so the\nleast-significant addition supplies the carry to the section. Widened\ncarry-zero sums supply group generate and reductions of operand XORs supply\ngroup propagate. Expanded carry equations drive the section masks and the\ncomparison carry. Signed comparison uses A's sign when the original operand\nsigns differ. The EX/MEM result register, forwarding, address generation,\nbranch comparison and MEM late-add retain their existing timing.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- A combinational SAT miter proved both ALU select modes equivalent to the\n  original operation results for all operand pairs and all 32 opcode values.\n  It also proved the all-zero registered select bundle produces zero.\n- All seven cocotb suites passed. The new tests exercise carries, borrows,\n  signed and unsigned comparisons, immediate compares, and forwarded operands.\n- The stock single-channel formal gate is running in a scratch copy.\n- Stock co-simulation passed for selftest and all three random traces with\n  and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed CRC validation with 10\n  iterations over 3,868,036 marker cycles.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Gowin placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Worst setup path |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| 0 | 92.076 | ID/EX rs1 data to the EX/MEM effective address |\n| 1 | 91.363 | Issue FIFO read pointer to the ID/EX shift-left select |\n| 2 | 91.363 | Issue FIFO read pointer to the ID/EX shift-left select |\n\nThe design uses 4,711 logic cells, down 50 from the champion. The 91.363 MHz\nmedian yields 236.20 CoreMark iterations/s and falls below the 101.226 MHz\npromotion threshold. Placement 0 also had MEM/WB forwarding paths through\nthe EX ALU within 0.01 ns of its worst setup path.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
