{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check; git status --short --ignored; git -C formal/riscv-formal status --short --untracked-files=no; sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/divider.sv\n!! .agent.last\n!! .agent.log\n!! cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n# Byte-sliced borrow lookahead in the divider\n\n## Implementation\n\n`rtl/divider.sv` uses one `trial_subtract` helper for the `D`, `2D`, and `3D` trials in each radix-4 digit. It splits the operands into four bytes and a two-bit upper slice. Unsigned less-than generates a borrow and equality propagates it. Expanded lookahead drives the byte multiplexers and returns the terminal borrow alongside the low 32 difference bits.\n\nEach byte with a variable incoming borrow computes `x - y` and `x + ~y` in parallel, modulo 256. The least significant byte specializes to `x - y` because its incoming borrow is always zero. The upper slice supplies only the terminal borrow. The divider executes two digits per work cycle with its original prefix and handoff schedule, one-hot selection, signed correction, and ALTOPS mode.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- All five divider cocotb tests passed, including signed and unsigned arithmetic, division by zero, overflow, fixed latency, result hold, and reset.\n- A combinational SAT proof checked the terminal borrow and low 32 bits against the original extended subtraction for all pairs of 34-bit operands.\n- The unchanged `bash formal/run_all.sh` gate passed all 53 checks on the first run using the bench core's single-channel ALTOPS configuration.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench` passed the selftest RVFI comparison with and without stalls and validated all stalled CoreMark CRCs.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\nThe three placement options measured 56.039, 54.582, and 54.582 MHz. The 54.582 MHz median is below the 80.77 MHz promotion threshold. At 4,233,123 marker cycles for ten iterations, the measured fitness was 128.94 iterations/s.\n\nFor placement option 0, the divider remained the critical path. The reported path used 24 cells, down from 73 in a local run of the original RTL. Its routing delay rose from 7.296 ns to 12.019 ns and offset the reduction in cell delay. Gowin reported 4,095 logic cells for the core, up from 3,237. Alternate borrow and result-mux formulations also fell below the promotion threshold in option 0.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
