{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_87", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; xs=[json.loads(line) for line in Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines() if line]; print({k:v for k,v in xs[-2].items() if k not in (\\\"proposed_change\\\", \\\"motivation\\\", \\\"files\\\", \\\"notes\\\", \\\"critical_path\\\")})' \"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261122-002-r8s1', 'title': 'Register fetch address candidates before steering', 'category': 'structural', 'hypothesis': {'motivation': 'The bench champion scores 216.99 iterations/s at a median 86.362 MHz over\\n3,979,945 CoreMark marker cycles. Its reported 16.665 ns Gowin path starts\\nat the synthetic instruction source and ends at the fetch request register.\\nThe direct target goes through target arithmetic, the aperture check, and\\nnext-PC selection before it reaches that register. A scratch implementation\\nwith separate full-width registers for all four address candidates preserved\\nthe marker count and reached 87.023 MHz median. Its critical path shifted\\nto the divider. Scratch variants that merged replay with the sequential\\nlane or retimed the FIFO squash scored lower. Keep the four distinct lanes\\nand reduce the speculative target lane to the address bits it can use.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Capture the predicted direct target, sequential successor, replay of the\\ncurrent request, and EX recovery word in parallel on each edge. Register\\nthe four mutually exclusive steering bits beside them and drive the next\\nrequest with a one-hot mux. Redirect has priority over normal acceptance.\\nDecode and the four-entry FIFO still receive the same applied prediction\\nand full architectural target, with same-edge squash and empty-queue\\nbypass on a corrected, ready response.\\n\\nThe speculative target lane only needs the 18 word-address bits inside the\\n1 MiB instruction aperture. Its enable decision checks the full computed\\ntarget and alignment before the lane can be selected. Keep full-width word\\naddresses for normal requests, EX recovery, and the target saved for EX\\ntraps and redirect. Select sequential on ordinary untaken acceptance\\nexcept at the last word, or when the held last-word instruction resolves\\nsequentially. Use replay on a stall, full FIFO, or aperture hold. Preserve\\nthe existing last-word hold and redirect priority.\\n\\nThis keeps target arithmetic and aperture qualification off the wide\\n\n…[4473 of 7545 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fc82756167bf3b1f]…\nider paths are within 0.002 ns of the ALU path.\\n\\nYosys equivalence checks against the champion passed for the fetch and execute stages. An additional bounded SAT check passed for fetch starting from reset. The stock single-channel `formal/run_all.sh` run was stopped near the end of the implementation budget with 8 of 53 checks complete, all passing. These included cover, liveness, illegal instruction, order uniqueness, backward PC, causality, ADDI, and AND. The run reported no counterexample or check failure before it was stopped.\\n', 'timestamp': '2026-11-22T08:26:52.884726Z', 'slot': 1, 'round_id': 8, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r8s1 (regression, +0.87%): Registering four fetch address candidates before one-hot selection with an 18-bit prediction lane left redirect and divider paths limiting the Gowin median to 78.081 MHz, and sharing the low 31-bit EX branch comparison raised it to 87.114 MHz with the registered EX ALU result critical in all three placements and CoreMark cycles unchanged.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
