{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(l) for l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\".join(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\", \\\"\\\") for r in rows[-3:]))'\"", "aggregated_output": "# Resolve the narrow divider digit in one radix-16 step\n\nThe narrow divider now consumes one nibble per work edge with 15 parallel 16-bit subtractions. Adjacent borrow bits select a single trial. The same selects encode the quotient digit and mask the low 11 bits of the remainder candidates. Initialization captures all divisor multiples, including the wide-mode products, under the initialization enable alone. Reset clears the phase and result state. A subsequent launch overwrites the products before the first work edge.\n\nThe lowest remainder bit combines the masks for even trial digits and for odd trial digits. Within each group, subtracting the corresponding multiple gives the same low bit. This grouping gave the best measured median. The leading-nibble initialization, seven work edges, final-edge handoff, pending result, wide radix-8 path, and signed and exceptional results are preserved.\n\nTests bracket every digit threshold and rollover for both quotient and remainder, including the signed cases at divisor magnitudes 15, 16, 2047, and 2048. The reset test checks a cleared result and relaunches with different divisors.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed. The divider preprocessed with `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` matched the champion byte for byte.\n- All seven cocotb suites passed. RVFI traces matched the ISS for selftest and three random programs with ready buses and with stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed UART validation in 3,979,945 marker cycles.\n- Local formal is incomplete within the implementation time budget. The unmodified single-retire ALTOPS gate and an additional parallel run of its generated checks returned 21 of 53 distinct passes at the last check. No failure or counterexample was reported. There were no RTL fix attempts for formal.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 83.109, 89.786, and 89.786 MHz with 4,684 logic cells and 1,034 registers. The 89.786 MHz median gives 225.60 CoreMark iter/s, 3.96% above the champion and below the 90.333 MHz promotion threshold. The EX redirect path t\n…[2979 of 6051 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2d95459761110b3b]…\n `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed selftest and all three random programs with both ready and stalled buses. Canonical stalled CoreMark passed all CRC checks and measured 3,868,036 marker cycles, down 2.81% from 3,979,945.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` confirmed that Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 reach 87.120, 96.774, and 96.774 MHz. The 96.774 MHz median clears the 87.793 MHz promotion threshold and scores 250.19 iterations/s, up 15.30% from 216.99. Option 0 was limited by EX forwarding into the data address. Options 1 and 2 were limited by the fetch recovery path into the next direct target. Gowin reported 4,761 logic cells and 1,148 registers, up from 4,224 and 954 for the champion.\n- Local formal was incomplete. The stock single-channel ALTOPS run generated 53 checks on the final RTL. Liveness, retirement uniqueness, backward PC consistency, and causality passed. The remaining checks had no result within the local budget. The run reported no counterexamples and required zero formal fix attempts.\n\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
