{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_138","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"date; find formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-wv8ui3CGq/checks -name status -exec head -q -n1 {} + | cut -d' ' -f1 | sort | uniq -c; git diff --check; cat cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"Sun Nov 22 14:34:08 CET 2026\n     11 PASS\n# Split direct targets across the fetch register\n\nFetch computes independent sums for byte-address bits `[7:2]` and `[19:8]` and builds a middle toggle mask from the PC/displacement XOR prefixes. The predicted request applies the registered low carry to the registered mask. A correctly predicted transfer can issue its target request on the next cycle.\n\nAperture qualification uses the middle generate or the middle propagate and low carry, then checks the current page against zero, one, or all ones. The acceptance logic also checks alignment and the gshare prediction. The FIFO and ID/EX carry the split target, carry and sign information, and the original alignment bit. EX reuses the packet PC's upper page and reconstructs all 32 target bits in parallel with branch comparison.\n\nThe pipeline cases check request addresses, retries and retirement cycles for forward and backward split carries, trained predictions rejected at both aperture edges, buffered transfers, misaligned and reserved encodings, a predicted request for the last word, and simultaneous MEM and EX recovery.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed. A Bitwuzla check proved the split arithmetic and aperture predicate equivalent to full-width addition over aligned PCs and signed 21-bit displacements.\n- All 58 pipeline cocotb cases and all six component suites passed.\n- Selftest and all three random programs passed RVFI cosim with both ready and stalled buses. Stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,868,036 marker cycles with canonical CRCs and the validation marker.\n- Local stock single-retire ALTOPS formal was incomplete. Of 53 generated checks, 11 passed, including cover, illegal-instruction detection, liveness, retirement uniqueness, and both PC-consistency checks. No counterexample was reported. There were zero formal fixes.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\nPlacement options 0, 1 and 2 reached 86.638, 94.169 and 94.169 MHz. The median yields 243.45 CoreMark iterations per second. The median is below the 101.23 MHz promotion threshold. The slowest paths ran from the FIFO pointer through issue control, from MEM/WB forwarding through the EX ALU, and through the divider recurrence. The placement 0 report counted 4,841 logic cells and 1,163 registers.\n\nExperiments that retimed FIFO issue control, selected ALU operands earlier, split the divider state, or moved the alternate address selection to MEM produced lower measured Fmax.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
