{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --check; git diff --stat; cat implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":" cores/bench/rtl/alu.sv            |  22 +++-\n cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           |   4 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |  10 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       |  43 +++++---\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv       |  23 ++--\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv       |   3 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv      |  14 ++-\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 218 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---\n 8 files changed, 291 insertions(+), 46 deletions(-)\n# Pipelined shifter and deferred bitwise completion\n\nEX reverses SLL operands, selects sign fill for SRA, and shifts by one and two. EX/MEM carries a 33-bit partial, three count bits, and direction. MEM shifts by four, eight, and sixteen and restores the SLL bit order before MEM/WB.\n\nThe issue stage classifies shifts and deferred ALU operations as late. ADD, AND, OR, XOR, and equality branches can consume the registered result in MEM. EX captures the ready operand and registers the one-hot completion controls when the producer actually writes. Two matching registers use doubling, pass-through, or zero as appropriate. A trapping producer uses the ordinary EX result. Encoded-only immediate matches repair the corresponding RVFI source value and leave the immediate calculation in EX.\n\nID also masks each register-file operand with its source select before capture. EX ORs the registered operand with the EX/MEM and MEM/WB bypass lanes. This placement measured a higher median than using the register-file select in EX.\n\nThe standalone ALU retains complete combinational shifts. The pipeline tests cover both shift encodings, encoded source aliases, trapped producers, x0, stalls, squash, the last fetch word, and dependent divide timing.\n\nVerilator lint and all seven cocotb runners passed. The stock cosim gate passed with CoreMark and all four ISS programs. Each ISS program ran with ready buses and with both stalls enabled. The cosim Make target needed `NRET=1` for the bench port set.\n\nBoth-stall CoreMark completed in 3,871,366 marker cycles, up 0.086% from the champion, with no out-of-bounds accesses. The seed, list, matrix, state, and final CRCs were `e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, and `fcaf`. UART reported “Correct operation validated.”\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 87.453, 93.185, and 93.185 MHz. The median yields 240.70 CoreMark iterations/s and falls short of the 103 MHz target. Fetch recovery limited option 0. Forwarding into address generation limited options 1 and 2, with nearby EX ALU, divider, and branch recovery paths.\n\nStock formal liveness, backwards PC continuity, and retirement uniqueness passed on the selected RTL. The full formal suite is still running.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
