{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && git check-ignore cores/bench/implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/divider.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_divider.py\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n# Registered divider operands\n\nLaunch captures the raw forwarded operands, both signed-operation sign flags, and the quotient or remainder selection. Phase 9 computes the magnitude, divisor multiples, and four-bit prefix. Phases 8 through 2 each consume two radix-4 digits. EX can hand off on the ninth edge, which registers the final arithmetic state. Phase 1 holds that state if acceptance is delayed. MEM selects and sign-corrects the result. ALTOPS captures the operands and opcode on launch and evaluates the existing substitute formula in phase 9 under the same handoff schedule.\n\nThe implementation follows the proposed schedule. The added edge makes the ready-bus retirement gap nine cycles after an immediately preceding instruction and ten cycles when a redirect or a late-result dependency inserts a bubble. A dependent integer consumer retires two cycles after the divide. The divider tests change the input operands and opcode immediately after launch and exercise reset before initialization, during recurrence, and with a held result.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed for the hardware and ALTOPS builds.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks, including liveness, on the first attempt.\n- All seven cocotb suites and all five cosimulation ELFs passed. The four trace ELFs passed with ready buses and with stalls.\n- Stalled CoreMark passed the canonical CRC and marker checks. Ten iterations took 4,233,123 cycles between the markers.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 60.059, 61.864, and 61.864 MHz. The median exceeds the 57.394 MHz acceptance threshold and projects to 146.14 iterations/s, 12.75% above the champion. The worst setup path in each placement ran from the register file through the integer ALU to dmem.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
