{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_88", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git diff --stat; sed -n '1,50p' bench/programs/Makefile; sed -n '130,165p' tools/eval/formal.py\"", "aggregated_output": " cores/bench/rtl/core.sv           |  11 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv       |  16 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv       |  17 +-\n cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv       |  21 ++-\n cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv       | 331 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------\n cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | 220 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-\n 6 files changed, 559 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)\nCROSS   := riscv32-unknown-elf\nCC      := $(CROSS)-gcc\n\n# CoreMark build knobs. Defaults are the canonical EEMBC reporting config\n# (2K data size, -O3); tools/eval/fpga.py's COREMARK_EXPECTED CRCs assume\n# exactly these defaults.\n# - COREMARK_SIZE: TOTAL_DATA_SIZE in coremark.h (#ifndef-guarded). 2000 is\n#   the EEMBC canonical reporting config (used by VexRiscv et al.); 6000\n#   makes the matrix/list/state working sets ~3x larger so the score is\n#   harder to inflate via register-resident working sets.\n# - COREMARK_OPT: gcc optimization. -O3 is the standard CoreMark publication\n#   flag; -O2 is what the V0 baseline used.\n# Defaults match VexRiscv's published CoreMark methodology so the\n# orchestrator's fitness number is directly comparable to public CoreMark\n# results. To override (e.g. for the prior 6K -O2 V0 baseline):\n#     make bench/programs/coremark.elf COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O2\nCOREMARK_SIZE ?= 2000\nCOREMARK_OPT  ?= -O3\n\nCFLAGS  := -march=rv32im -mabi=ilp32 $(COREMARK_OPT) -static -nostartfiles \\\n           -specs=nano.specs -specs=nosys.specs \\\n           -T bench/programs/link.ld -Ibench/programs/coremark \\\n           -Ibench/programs/coremark/baremetal \\\n           -DTOTAL_DATA_SIZE=$(COREMARK_SIZE)\n\nSRCS := bench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_matrix.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_state.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/core_util.c \\\n        bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.c \\\n        bench/programs/crt0.S\n\nbench/programs/coremark.elf: $(SRCS)\n\t$(CC) $(CFLAGS) $^ -o $@\n\nbench/programs/selftest.elf: bench/prog\n…[1652 of 4724 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3bcd83a5b0e87afa]…\nkills the rep\n            # (round_id stays at whatever round was in flight, the\n            # orchestrator's main loop dies, and the rep finalizes at iter=N\n            # instead of running its full N=15). Observed live on\n            # deepseek-v4-pro reps where some hypotheses produced SMT\n            # problems that bitwuzla couldn't close in 30 minutes.\n            # Return a slot-broken outcome with a recognizable error class\n            # so the report's broken_by_class table surfaces it cleanly.\n            # run_pgroup preserves text=True, so e.stdout/e.stderr arrive as\n            # str. (subprocess.run with text=True would behave the same way,\n            # the prior .decode() call was always latent, but TimeoutExpired\n            # never fired in practice under the 30-min ceiling so it stayed\n            # hidden until kimi-rep3 hit the bumped 45-min ceiling and an\n            # AttributeError crashed the orchestrator. See commit bfe9f84.)\n            partial = (e.stdout or \"\") + (e.stderr or \"\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
