{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'tail -3 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r12s0\", \"title\": \"Predecode divider magnitude carries on the launch edge\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"In Gowin placements 1 and 2, the champion's divider path from dividend\\nbit 0 to the initializing remainder is within 0.012 ns of the longest\\nreported data arrival. Initialization reduces the low 28 captured\\ndividend bits to form a signed top nibble, then uses the nibble to read\\nthe prefix quotient and remainder tables. It also decodes the signed\\ndivisor's table row. The launch edge can capture these inputs to shorten\\nboth paths into the tables.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"In Gowin placements 1 and 2, the champion's divider path from dividend\\nbit 0 to the initializing remainder is within 0.012 ns of the longest\\nreported data arrival. Initialization reduces the low 28 captured\\ndividend bits to form a signed top nibble, then uses the nibble to read\\nthe prefix quotient and remainder tables. It also decodes the signed\\ndivisor's table row. The launch edge can capture these inputs to shorten\\nboth paths into the tables.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Capture whether the low 28 dividend bits are nonzero and the one-hot\\ndivisor row on the same edge as the raw operands. In initialization,\\nnegate the high dividend nibble using the registered low-word zero flag\\nas its carry-in. Use the registered divisor row to select the existing\\nprefix quotient and remainder table entries. Continue to gate table use\\nby the full divisor magnitude and preserve the other dividend bits, the\\nseven work edges, and the final-edge or pending handoff. Keep the ALTOPS\\npath and all RV32M exceptional results intact.\\n\\nA scratch build that captured only the dividend flag reached 91.615 MHz\\nmedian, with recovery into the FIFO write por