{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat formal/checks_si.cfg; rg -n 'aperture|100000|oob|gw_sh|GOWIN|TemporaryDirectory|build_dir|coremark' tools/eval/gowin.py tools/eval/cosim.py tools/eval/fpga.py test/cosim/main.cpp bench/programs/Makefile; cat test/cosim/build.sh\"", "aggregated_output": "[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\nbench/programs/Makefile:7:# - COREMARK_SIZE: TOTAL_DATA_SIZE in coremark.h (#ifndef-guarded). 2000 is\nbench/programs/Makefile:16:#     make bench/programs/coremark.elf COREMARK_SIZE=6000 COREMARK_OPT=-O2\nbench/programs/Makefile:22:           -T bench/programs/link.ld -Ibench/programs/coremark \\\nbench/programs/Makefile:23:           -Ibench/programs/coremark/baremetal \\\nbench/programs/Makefile:26:SRCS := bench/programs/coremark/core_list_join.c \\\nbench/programs/Makefile:27:        bench/programs/coremark/core_main.c \\\nbench/programs/Makefile:28:        bench/programs/coremark/core_matrix.c \\\nbench\n…[7198 of 10270 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7ca86985e1217ed5]…\nRET:-2}\"\n\n# Ensure OSS CAD Suite tools are on PATH for non-interactive shells.\nTOOLCHAIN=\"$REPO_ROOT/.toolchain\"\nif [ -d \"$TOOLCHAIN/oss-cad-suite/bin\" ]; then\n  export PATH=\"$TOOLCHAIN/oss-cad-suite/bin:$PATH\"\nfi\n\nmkdir -p \"$OBJ_DIR\"\n\n# Glob $RTL_DIR/*.sv. core_pkg.sv first; the rest in a stable lexicographic\n# order (modulo case-insensitive sort, which Verilator/gcc don't care\n# about). If core_pkg.sv is missing the build will catch that downstream\n# via undefined-typedef errors.\nRTL_FILES=()\n[ -f \"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\" ] && RTL_FILES+=(\"$RTL_DIR/core_pkg.sv\")\nfor f in \"$RTL_DIR\"/*.sv; do\n  [ \"$(basename \"$f\")\" = \"core_pkg.sv\" ] && continue\n  RTL_FILES+=(\"$f\")\ndone\n\nif [ ${#RTL_FILES[@]} -eq 0 ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: no rtl/*.sv files found.\" >&2\n  exit 1\nfi\n\nverilator --cc --exe --build \\\n  -Mdir \"$OBJ_DIR\" \\\n  \"+incdir+$RTL_DIR\" \\\n  --top-module core \\\n  -Wall -Wno-fatal -Wno-style \\\n  -CFLAGS \"-DNRET=$NRET\" \\\n  \"${RTL_FILES[@]}\" \\\n  \"$COSIM_DIR/main.cpp\" \\\n  -o cosim_sim\n\necho \"Built: $OBJ_DIR/cosim_sim\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
