{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; data=json.loads(Path(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").read_text().splitlines()[-1]); print(data.keys()); print({k:v for k,v in data.items() if k not in (\\\"motivation\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"lessons\\\",\\\"description\\\")})'\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n{'id': 'hyp-20261122-003-r4s2', 'category': 'predictor', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 15, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add the four-entry packed-vector ring with a free-tail write enable, logical enqueue and dequeue pointers, and an empty-queue bypass. Advance the request PC on response acceptance. Defer speculative fall-through at the aperture edge and give EX recovery priority.'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Use fetch-packet validity for the late-result interlock. Signal decode consumption independently of imem readiness and retain the existing load-use bubble, divide hold and dmem hold priorities.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect decode consumption and packet validity to the predictor queue and hazard unit. Keep the existing EX redirect and training signals.'}, {'file': 'rtl/id_stage.sv', 'description': 'Clear only ID/EX validity on reset or squash. Capture the packet payload whenever the existing decode hold is deasserted.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check queue wraparound, full-queue backpressure and ordered drain during imem stalls. Extend stalled-branch recovery to discard buffered wrong-path stores. Exercise a cold taken branch at the last imem word. Retain branch training, retirement order and exact divider gap checks.'}], 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 145.58, 'delta_pct': 12.31, 'vs_baseline': 1101.16, 'fmax_mhz': 57.942, 'ipc_coremark': 3e-06, 'cycles': 3979945, 'iterations': 10, 'lut4': 3645, 'ff': 746, 'seeds': [55.382, 57.942, 57.942], 'perturbations': [[0, 55.382, 16], \n…[2685 of 5757 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9e0226d55a9f0c77]…\nn- `make timing TARGET=bench` passed. `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` reproduced the three placement frequencies of 55.382, 57.942, and 57.942 MHz. The 57.942 MHz median gives 145.58 CoreMark iterations/s, 12.32% above the champion. Bracketed cycles fell by 5.98%. Gowin reported 3,645 logic cells, 746 registers, and 33 distributed RAM cells.\\n\\nThe limiting reported paths run through EX recovery to the fetch PC and ID/EX validity. The median is 3.981 MHz above the 53.961 MHz qualification frequency at the measured cycle count.\\n', 'timestamp': '2026-11-22T04:13:04.227432Z', 'slot': 2, 'round_id': 4, 'lesson': '- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r4s2 (regression, +12.31%): A four-entry LUT-RAM fetch queue cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 5.98% by fetching during decode holds, with registered occupancy isolating its write enable from EX recovery and the remaining recovery paths to the fetch PC and ID/EX valid bit limiting median Gowin Fmax to 57.942 MHz, leaving throughput 0.56 iterations/s behind the round winner.'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
