{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'tail -6 formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-registeredrecovery/checks/reg_ch0/logfile.txt; nl -ba cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'","aggregated_output":"SBY  5:38:38 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Skipping step 17..\nSBY  5:38:38 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Skipping step 18..\nSBY  5:38:38 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Skipping step 19..\nSBY  5:38:38 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:01  Checking assumptions in step 20..\nSBY  5:38:41 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:00:03  Checking assertions in step 20..\nSBY  5:39:41 [reg_ch0] engine_0: ##   0:01:03  waiting for solver (1 minute)\n     1\t# Registered branch recovery\n     2\t\n     3\tEX forms a single alternate word address from the saved prediction or the forwarded JALR sum. IF registers that address every cycle alongside separate direction-miss and aperture-resume bits. The registered recovery state selects the imem and gshare request, masks the younger ID/EX packet, and presents the response directly to decode. On the next edge, IF rebases the queue and advances from an accepted response or retains the recovery PC for retry. RVFI continues to report the full resolved successor, and each advancing conditional branch trains its saved gshare index once.\n     4\t\n     5\tThe four-entry FIFO uses an asynchronous-read, synchronous-write packed-vector array. Its registered head and tail pointers determine physical write eligibility. A full queue resumes accepting responses on the cycle after a pop. Decode can drain the queue during imem backpressure, and fetch can fill it during dmem and divide holds. The last imem word issues through the empty bypass and waits for EX if its prediction is sequential.\n     6\t\n     7\tThe implementation also uses one-hot EX forwarding selects with the existing producer priority. The registered-recovery design with the original forwarding mux measured 60.380 MHz median. The one-hot mux raised the median above the 60.84 MHz hurdle. The longest paths still run from the register file through the EX ALU to dmem.\n     8\t\n     9\t## Local verification\n    10\t\n    11\t- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All 87 cocotb cases passed, including 27 pipeline cases. Coverage includes full-queue behavior, stalled training and recovery, wrong-path store and divide discard, aperture-edge retry and resume, and the existing exact divider and retirement-order checks.\n    12\t- The first formal run found a `pc_fwd_ch0` counterexample where retirement 7 used PC `0x00000000` after retirement 6 reported successor `0x00000004`. Yosys elaborated the struct-array FIFO as a single register. Declaring the FIFO storage as a plain packed-vector array fixed the counterexample, and the rerun passed all 53 single-issue ALTOPS checks.\n    13\t- Selftest and three random programs passed full RVFI comparison in both bus modes. Stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,979,945 marker-bracketed cycles with all canonical CRCs and no out-of-bounds accesses.\n    14\t- Gowin measured 61.096, 64.667, and 64.667 MHz across placement options 0, 1, and 2. The 64.667 MHz median gives 162.48 iterations/s, 11.18% above the 146.14 iterations/s champion. Gowin reported 3,626 logic cells, 844 registers, and 33 distributed RAM cells.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
