{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_41", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(l)\n if 'r8s' in d['id']:\n  print(d['id'], d.keys())\n  print(str(d.get('fpga', {}))[:2400])\n  print(str(d.get('implementation_notes',''))[:2200])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-001-r8s0 dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n{}\n# Parallel branch comparisons\n\nEX compares the four bytes of the forwarded operands in parallel. The top-byte ordering comparison flips both sign bits for signed branches. Each less-than flag is qualified by equality of every higher byte, and whole-word equality uses the same four equality flags. The decoded `funct3` selects the predicate and its polarity.\n\nThe predicate feeds redirect and FIFO recovery, the RVFI successor, and predictor training on the existing EX decision edge. The decoder validates the branch encoding, and EX applies the existing stall and target-alignment checks. The RTL follows the proposed comparator. The pipeline test adds all six branch encodings with equal operands, signed limits, and first differences in each byte. It checks RVFI operand values, the reported successor, and the retirement path.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint passed.\n- A Yosys SAT check proved the EX predicate equivalent to full-width comparisons for all operand pairs and all six legal branch encodings.\n- A separate ALTOPS-mode induction check proved cycle-by-cycle equivalence to the original EX stage for all decoded branch operations. It compared the registered state and all EX outputs, including redirect, training, and the EX/MEM payload.\n- `make test TARGET=bench` passed all seven cocotb runners.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed for five ELFs. The four trace programs matched with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed UART validation at 3,979,945 marker cycles.\n- The single-channel `formal/run_all.sh` suite remained incomplete at the local verification cutoff. All 24 co\n…[4781 of 7853 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:854eb8bc9a3319da]…\nLocal verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall`.\n- All seven cocotb runners passed, including 45 pipeline cases. The replay cases cover both endpoint block tags, FIFO backpressure, ready-response priority, descriptor replacement, loop exit, and FENCE.I advance and squash.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and the three random programs with and without memory stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed CRC validation in 3,755,433 marker cycles, 5.64% fewer than the champion's 3,979,945 cycles.\n- Gowin measured 74.696, 80.894, and 80.894 MHz across the three placement options. The median of 80.894 MHz fell short of the 85.238 MHz promotion target. The slowest paths reach the issue-valid register and the FIFO pointer resets through recovery and issue control.\n- The first formal invocation stopped in Yosys parsing at the loop RAM width declaration. Applying `$bits` to a declared signal, as the existing FIFO does, resolved the error. The full suite remained incomplete within the local time budget. The causal, cove\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
