{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python -B - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nitem = json.loads(Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261122-003-r14s2.log').read_text().splitlines()[279])['item']\nprint(item.get('aggregated_output', '')[:12500])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? cores/bench/test/test_fetch_replay.py\n# Branch-trained resident instruction store\n\nFetch retains a four-entry flow-through queue and uses eight physical live\nslots. An accepted live response can stage a decoded payload for one of 512\ndirect-mapped resident slots. Taken conditional branches from EX and late MEM\ntrain a 64-bit bitmap of 64-byte blocks. The older eligible MEM observation\nhas priority. Exact word tags and in-RAM validity qualify replay.\n\nReplay queues a resident slot, the current gshare prediction, and narrow\noperand hints. The hints keep register reads and the issue interlock off the\nwide resident payload path. Two synchronous payload copies read the queued\nsuccessor and the incoming candidate in parallel. The queue pins referenced\nslots through the pop edge. A held resident head retains its payload.\n\nThe live FIFO uses distributed RAM. The direction and target-eligibility\nregisters keep the fetch target range check separate from the gshare path.\nID captures payload and operand selects whenever EX can advance, using its\nvalid bit to represent dependency bubbles.\n\nReady responses retain priority and the empty bypass. Recovery discards\nyounger references, and the last aperture word waits for EX on every live\nacceptance. Accepting FENCE.I clears admission and restarts a 256-edge\nparallel metadata scrub. Outstanding fences suppress new resident activity\nuntil they advance or recovery discards them.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint, ready and stalled ISS selftest traces, and the canonical\n  CoreMark CRC gate passed. The measured stall run took 3,407,072 marker\n  cycles for ten iterations, 11.92% below 3,868,036. UART reported seed,\n  list, matrix, state, and final CRCs of `0xe9f5`, `0xe714`, `0x1fd7`,\n  `0x8e3a`, and `0xfcaf` and confirmed correct operation.\n- All eight cocotb runners passed. Directed tests exercise exact tag aliases,\n  parity lookahead across a resident index wrap, pinned fills, stalled candidate\n  conflicts, parallel reads, live priority, fence invalidation and accounting,\n  and recovery into DIV/REM with the retirement gap check.\n- The first formal invocation hit a Yosys parser error on `$bits(type)`.\n  Replacing those expressions with `$bits(signal)` fixed elaboration.\n  The single-retire checks are running.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Revision | Option 0 | Option 1 | Option 2 | Median |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Initial parallel resident reads | 71.408 MHz | 73.716 MHz | 73.716 MHz | 73.716 MHz |\n| Fabric operand hints and distributed live FIFO | 73.661 MHz | 83.944 MHz | 83.944 MHz | 83.944 MHz |\n| Split live direction and target eligibility (retained) | 88.375 MHz | 88.564 MHz | 88.564 MHz | 88.564 MHz |\n| Shared JALR and load/store address adder | 70.851 MHz | 74.628 MHz | 74.628 MHz | 74.628 MHz |\n\nThe 88.564 MHz median gives 259.94 iterations/s, 3.90% above the champion\nat 96.774 MHz and 3,868,036 cycles. It falls 0.599 MHz below the\n89.163 MHz promotion threshold. This revision used 5,666 logic cells,\n1,619 registers, and 16 block RAMs. Its worst path runs from the selected\nMEM/WB operand through the EX ALU. The live FIFO write path after replay\nsteering was within 0.004 ns of the worst path in options 1 and 2.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
