{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261122-002-r7s1\\\"|\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261122-001-r6s0\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"],d[\\\"critical_path\\\"]) for l in sys.stdin for d in [json.loads(l.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1])]]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-001-r6s0 Split each 34-bit trial subtraction in radix4_step into four byte slices\nand a two-bit upper slice. For each byte, compute the low result for both\npossible incoming borrows in parallel with local borrow generation and\nequality. Use explicit group lookahead from the slice generate and\npropagate signals to drive the byte result muxes and the final trial\nborrow. For a slice, unsigned less-than generates a borrow and equality\npropagates it. The upper slice contributes only to the final borrow.\nThis gives Gowin short local carry chains in both radix-4 digits and puts\ngroup lookahead in parallel with local difference calculation.\n\nKeep both digits per work cycle, the existing prefix and handoff schedule,\nand the ALTOPS branch. Give each trial exactly the same low 32 bits and\nterminal borrow as the original extended subtraction. Preserve the\none-hot digit selection, signed correction, divide-by-zero and overflow\nresults, and result hold under backpressure. Verify the arithmetic and\nhandshake with the existing divider suite and run the unchanged formal\nand stalled CoreMark gates. At the same marker count, the promotion\nthreshold is 80.77 MHz. Estimate 85 MHz and about 201 iterations/s if\nthe divider path shortens and the next path meets timing.\n {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_divider/divisor_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_divider/remainder_q_3_s0', 'slack_ns': -12.845, 'arrival_ns': 23.139, 'logic_cells': 24, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_divider']}\nhyp-20261122-002-r7s1 Put the existing decoder and immediate generator on the imem response\nside of a four-entry, flow-through issue FIFO. Store the decoded\ncontrol and full immediate alongside the raw instruction, PC, full\ndirect target, applied prediction and lookup index. Use a\npacked-vector array with an asynchronous head read, a synchronous\ntail write qualified by response acceptance, and wrap-bit read and\nwrite pointers. Keep register reads, WB collision capture and\nproducer matching at issue, using the selected packet's encoded\nsource tags.\n\nWith room and a ready response, accept the packet and advance the\nrequest PC even if issue is held. Issue may drain the oldest queued\npacket during imem backpressure. When empty, let the decoded response\nbypass the FIFO. A bypass accepted directly by issue advances both\npointers, leaving the FIFO empty. A full queue resumes accepting\nimem responses on the cycle after a pop. A load-use bubble keeps the\nsame head for retry. During divide or dmem holds, stop issue and\ncontinue accepting fetches while space is available.\n\nUse the champion's EX redirect directly to discard younger FIFO\nentries, clear ID/EX validity and update the request PC on the same\nedge, including during imem backpressure. Reset invalidates the queue\nby clearing its pointers. At the last word of the 1 MiB imem window,\na sequential prediction may accept the packet once. Hold the request\nthere and deassert response acceptance until that PC advances in EX\nor an older redirect arrives. Use the resolved successor when\nresuming. Keep the gshare and JAL prediction rules and train once on\neach advancing conditional branch using the index saved with its\nown packet. Preserve validated decoder defaults, memory side effects,\nsingle-channel RVFI and the existing EX and RV32M schedules.\n\nThe prototype passed canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,979,945\nmarker cycles, down 5.98%. Gowin placement options 0 through 2\nreached 84.531, 86.633 and 86.633 MHz. The median gives 217.67\niter/sec, up 7.97%. The 4.6% acceptance margin at this cycle count\nrequires about 83.927 MHz. The prototype passed eight RVFI trace\ncomparisons across selftest and three random ELFs in both bus modes,\nall 97 cocotb cases with the updated fetch assertions, and the\nsingle-channel formal liveness check. Run the full unchanged formal\nsuite and remeasure the tournament implementation.\n {'from': 'lfsr_4_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/request_word_q_18_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.371, 'arrival_ns': 16.665, 'logic_cells': 34, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
