{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261122-002-r10s1|hyp-20261122-001-r10s0|hyp-20261122-001-r9s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys,pprint; rows=map(json.loads,sys.stdin); keys=(\\\"id\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"perturbations\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\"); [pprint.pp({k:r[k] for k in keys if k in r},width=140) for r in rows]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261122-001-r9s0',\n 'fitness': 224.08,\n 'fmax_mhz': 89.183,\n 'cycles': 3979945,\n 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.result_2_s0',\n                   'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.valid_s0',\n                   'slack_ns': -7.08,\n                   'arrival_ns': 17.374,\n                   'logic_cells': 38,\n                   'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']},\n 'perturbations': [[0, 82.781, 13], [1, 89.183, 14], [2, 89.183, 14]],\n 'implementation_notes': '# Predecode EX result selection and share the right shifter\\n'\n                         '\\n'\n                         'ID predecodes the integer result lanes and captures their enables and the arithmetic fill bit with the ID/EX '\n                         'payload. Payload capture follows `issue_candidate`, including on the redirect edge where `issue` clears '\n                         'validity. Both right shifts use one signed 33-bit shift. The extra high bit is `arithmetic_fill & a[31]`, and '\n                         'the result lane takes the low 32 bits. A separate left shifter feeds the same masked-OR mux as the right '\n                         'shifter. The encoded `alu` wrapper uses the shared datapath.\\n'\n                         '\\n'\n                         'JAL and JALR select PC+4 as their sole result lane. The EX alignment check still qualifies the link for '\n                         'forwarding and writeback. Address generation, branch comparison, RV32M and RVFI source capture continue to '\n                         'consume the ordinary forwarded operands.\\n'\n                         '\\n'\n                         'The pipeline tests cover immediate and register SLL, SRL and SRA on a negative operand at counts 0, 1, 16 and '\n                         '31. They check forwarded register counts with populated upper bits, adjacent retirement, a held SRA followed by '\n                         'a queued SRL, JAL/JALR link consumers, and alignment traps that preserve the destination register.\\n'\n                         '\\n'\n    \n…[11695 of 14767 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:9256e5bf64917af1]…\n.\\n'\n                         '- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` confirmed that Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 reach 87.120, 96.774, and 96.774 MHz. '\n                         'The 96.774 MHz median clears the 87.793 MHz promotion threshold and scores 250.19 iterations/s, up 15.30% from '\n                         '216.99. Option 0 was limited by EX forwarding into the data address. Options 1 and 2 were limited by the fetch '\n                         'recovery path into the next direct target. Gowin reported 4,761 logic cells and 1,148 registers, up from 4,224 '\n                         'and 954 for the champion.\\n'\n                         '- Local formal was incomplete. The stock single-channel ALTOPS run generated 53 checks on the final RTL. '\n                         'Liveness, retirement uniqueness, backward PC consistency, and causality passed. The remaining checks had no '\n                         'result within the local budget. The run reported no counterexamples and required zero formal fix attempts.\\n'}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
