{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'recovery path|alu_result.*mem_addr|\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; keys=(\\\"id\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"perturbations\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\"); [print(*(r.get(k) for k in keys),sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "baseline-bench-00eedbd\n{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -189.542, 'arrival_ns': 199.837, 'logic_cells': 156, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n[[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]]\nNone\nhyp-20261122-001-r1s0\n{'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_divrem/remainder_q_5_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_divrem/remainder_q_11_s0', 'slack_ns': -20.237, 'arrival_ns': 30.531, 'logic_cells': 127, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_divrem']}\n[[0, 39.625, 33], [1, 39.19, 32], [2, 39.19, 32]]\n{'motivation': 'The baseline reaches 5.442 MHz and its 199.837 ns worst path traverses\\nforwarding and the EX ALU across 156 logic cells. The signed and unsigned\\ncombinational divide and remainder operators are the strongest candidate\\nfor that depth. Sharing and registering the division recurrence should\\nraise the clock rate for every instruction, with a direct cycle cost\\nconfined to DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU. A baseline Verilator run with both\\nstall streams reproduced all canonical CoreMark CRCs and the 4,491,485\\ncycles between markers. Its 2,922,015 retirements inside that window\\ncontained zero divide or remainder instructions.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Replace all four combinational division operators with one fixed-latency\\nrestoring divider. Latch the forwarded operands and operation on launch.\\nIn a setup cycle form unsigned magnitudes and 34-bit divisor multiples\\nD, 2D, and 3D. Each radix-4 step shifts two dividend bits into the\\nremainder, computes three 35-bit candidate differences in parallel, and\\nuses their borrow bits to select the largest fitting multiple and its\\nquotient digit.\\nReuse four cascaded steps over four registered rounds to produce the\\n32-bit quotient and remainder. Select and sign-correct the result for\\nEX/MEM on the following cycle. The fixed sequence adds six EX cycles\\nper divide or remainder. Preserve truncation toward zero, the dividend's\\nsign on signed remainder, and the specified zero-divisor and INT_MIN/-1\\nresults on t\n…[55103 of 58175 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8a3a38f1218969a7]…\nun budget. Recheck all placements,\\ncomplete the existing single-issue formal gate, and exercise stalled\\nrecovery and speculative fence squash.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 10, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Add the banked loop predictor and registered replay lane. Decouple physical FIFO writes from tail acceptance, qualify the aperture hold with registered recovery, and split live target arithmetic at the aperture boundary.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export the branch PC and exact direct target alongside the existing branch advance and direction signals. Export an advancing FENCE.I pulse.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Connect the backedge and fence observations to fetch while preserving the single-channel interface.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Add replay tests for consecutive stalled beats, bank and tag boundaries, FIFO pressure, redirects, fence invalidation and retirement order.'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
