en\nby registered state. EX still computes the full resolved successor for\nRVFI and applies the existing alignment trap and link-write suppression.\n\nThe registered recovery pulse masks the younger ID/EX packet's validity\nbefore it can execute, train, or cause an interlock. It also treats the FIFO\nas empty, so a ready response at the recovery address can enter ID/EX via\nthe bypass immediately. At the following edge, rebase the FIFO pointers to\n…[3950 of 7022 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:18ab2112ab7a985a]…\ny response.\n\nThe speculative target lane only needs the 18 word-address bits inside the\n1 MiB instruction aperture. Its enable decision checks the full computed\ntarget and alignment before the lane can be selected. Keep full-width word\naddresses for normal requests, EX recovery, and the target saved for EX\ntraps and redirect. Select sequential on ordinary untaken acceptance\nexcept at the last word, or when the held last-word instruction resolves\nsequentially. Use replay on a stall, full FIFO, or aperture hold. Preserve\nthe existing last-word hold and redirect priority.\n\nThis keeps target arithmetic and aperture qualification off the wide\nnext-address data mux before the register. The reduced direct lane removes\nspeculative high-bit flops and mux inputs. At the current marker cycle count, the\npromotion margin requires a median above 90.33 MHz. A 91.5 MHz median would\nyield about 230 iterations/s. Divider or ALU timing can still cap the gain,\nso measure all three Gowin placements and confirm the marker count.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
