{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261122-002-r10s1|hyp-20261122-001-r9s0|hyp-20261122-001-r13s0|hyp-20261122-002-r13s1|hyp-20261122-002-r12s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json; keys=(\\\"id\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"seeds\\\",\\\"perturbations\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\"); [print(json.dumps({k:r.get(k) for k in keys},indent=2)) for l in sys.stdin if (r:=json.loads(l))]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r9s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Predecode EX result selection and share the right shifter\",\n  \"fitness\": 224.08,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 89.183,\n  \"cycles\": 3979945,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    82.781,\n    89.183,\n    89.183\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      82.781,\n      13\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      89.183,\n      14\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      89.183,\n      14\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.result_2_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.valid_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -7.08,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 17.374,\n    \"logic_cells\": 38,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The champion has an 11.327 ns path from ID/EX operand bit 9 to EX/MEM ALU result bit 5, consistent with a right shift feeding a late result mux. In r8s1 the ALU result was a timing limit in all three Gowin placements. A scratch implementation of one-hot result selection alone reached 86.711 MHz median. Reducing the result fan-in and redundant shifter wiring is the remaining opportunity.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Register one-hot EX result enables alongside the decoded operation at issue. Merge SRL and SRA into one right-shift result lane with a registered arithmetic-fill bit. Implement the shared lane as a signed 33-bit right shift with the extra high bit set to arithmetic_fill AND operand_a[31], then retain the low 32 bits. Retain a dedicated left-shift lane so either direction has at most one barrel shift before the ALU result selection. The smaller output mux takes PC+4 as a mutually exclusive lane for JAL and JALR, removing the serial jump-link mux. Existing address, comparator and RV32M inputs continue to use the ordinary forwarding datapath.\\n\\nCapture result enables and fill mode with the ID/EX payload under the existing issue, hold and squash rules. Keep the standalone encoded ALU interface for unit tests by deriving the same enables from its opcode. Preserve the qualified link write after alignment checking, RVFI source values and all current \n…[35966 of 39038 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7460aa41e7895417]…\necks remain unverified. The logs show solver waits and no counterexample, so no formal repair retries were made.\\n\\n## Gowin timing\\n\\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Block RAMs | Worst setup path |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\\n| 0 | 82.137 | 4 | ID/EX rs2 forwarding select through the ALU to EX/MEM result |\\n| 1 | 90.676 | 4 | EX/MEM result through forwarding and the ALU back to EX/MEM result |\\n| 2 | 90.676 | 4 | EX/MEM result through forwarding and the ALU back to EX/MEM result |\\n\\nThe 90.676 MHz median yields 234.42 CoreMark iterations/s, below the 101.23 MHz promotion threshold at this cycle count. Gowin reports 4,807 logic cells and 1,198 registers, an increase of 46 cells and 50 registers over the champion. The address-sum and upper-correction endpoints fall outside the 25 worst setup paths in each report. Option 0 also has MEM recovery into ID/EX within 0.003 ns of its limiting ALU path. Options 1 and 2 show divider remainder feedback and recovery within 0.031 ns of the limiting setup slack.\\n\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
