-hot EX result enables alongside the decoded operation at issue. Merge SRL and SRA into one right-shift result lane with a registered arithmetic-fill bit. Implement the shared lane as a signed 33-bit right shift with the extra high bit set to arithmetic_fill AND operand_a[31], then retain the low 32 bits. Retain a dedicated left-shift lane so either direction has at most one barrel shift before the ALU result selection. The smaller output mux takes PC+4 as a mutually exclusive lane for JAL and JALR, removing the serial jump-link mux. Existing address, comparator and RV32M inputs continue to use the ordinary forwarding datapath.\\n\\nCapture result enables and fill mode with the ID/EX payload under the existing issue, hold and squash rul\n…[29760 of 32832 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7f10b01219101aa5]…\nts separately from the other ALU results for the fused issue selection while retaining standalone ALU behavior.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export fast result lanes and consume the captured operands with only the registered MEM/WB bypass. Preserve writeback and late completion routing.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Feed fast values back to the issue snapshots and preserve stage hold, producer qualification, recovery and RVFI wiring.'}]} # Capture fast producer values on the consumer’s issue edge\n\nID/EX captures each encoded source from the youngest eligible EX writer or the write-first register file. A MEM match registers a MEM/WB select and leaves the snapshot zero. The separate ALU B snapshot inserts the immediate during issue. Encoded rs2 retains its full value for stores, branches, RV32M and RVFI.\n\nThe issue muxes apply tag-qualified masks directly to the unmasked ADD and SUB results. A shared lane carries the other ALU results, jump links and AUIPC. EX/MEM merges the same\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
