{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"agent_message","text":"Wrote and schema-validated one `micro_opt` hypothesis for `cores/bench`. It replaces the combinational DIV and REM datapaths with a shared radix-4 divider that adds six execute cycles per operation. [hyp-20261122-001-r1s0.yaml](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-001-r1s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r1s0.yaml)\n\nThe baseline CoreMark run matched all canonical CRCs and retired zero divide or remainder instructions inside the timing window. The projected **+50% fitness** requires about **8.17 MHz** at the baseline cycle count and awaits Gowin measurement."}}
