{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_1", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md && rg -n -i 'micro_opt|multipli|dsp|alu' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-001-r1s0 (regression, +619.88%): Replacing combinational DIV/REM on the shared EX path with registered radix-4 rounds raised median Fmax from 5.442 to 39.190 MHz, with four cascaded steps per round setting the new timing limit and CoreMark's divide-free marker window staying at 4,491,485 cycles.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r1s1 (improvement, +729.13%): Reducing the shared divider from four cascaded radix-4 steps per cycle to three moved the critical path out of the divider and raised median Gowin Fmax from 39.190 to 45.134 MHz, with a nine-cycle retirement gap after a redirect or load-use bubble on ready buses still within the ten-cycle liveness bound.\n- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +3.96%): A fetch-local 16-entry tagged BTB saved 5.73% of CoreMark cycles by avoiding redirect bubbles on correct predictions, with the EX ALU still on the critical path and a drop in median post-placement Fmax from 5.442 to 5.334 MHz limiting the throughput gain.\n1:{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-00eedbd\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T02:36:30.621996Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n2:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Fold DIV and REM into a shared radix-4 unit\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches 5.442 MHz and its 199.837 ns worst path traverses\\nforwardin\n…[29236 of 32308 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d95c7187b4d40ad3]…\nlidation checks under imem and dmem stalls.\\n\\n## Tournament build measurements\\n\\n| Metric | Recorded baseline | BTB |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| CoreMark bracketed cycles for 10 iterations | 4,491,485 | 4,234,052 |\\n| Gowin median Fmax | 5.442 MHz | 5.334 MHz |\\n| CoreMark iterations per second | 12.12 | 12.60 |\\n\\nGowin reported 4.908, 5.334, and 5.334 MHz for placement options 0, 1, and 2. Option 0 used 12,665 logic cells, 509 registers, and 21 LUT-RAM cells. The longest setup path still crosses the EX ALU, and the lower median Fmax offsets part of the 5.73% cycle reduction. The measured throughput gain is 3.97%.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T02:58:44.049874Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +3.96%): A fetch-local 16-entry tagged BTB saved 5.73% of CoreMark cycles by avoiding redirect bubbles on correct predictions, with the EX ALU still on the critical path and a drop in median post-placement Fmax from 5.442 to 5.334 MHz limiting the throughput gain.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
