{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_71", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,220p' formal/run_all.sh && ls -ld formal/riscv-formal && ls -la formal\"", "aggregated_output": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Run riscv-formal checks against the current $RTL_DIR/*.sv.\n# Requires: formal/riscv-formal cloned (manual clone or `git submodule init`).\n#\n# Stages every $RTL_DIR/*.sv plus wrapper.sv + the chosen checks config under\n# the riscv-formal tree, then runs sby -> bitwuzla via the framework's\n# generated makefile. Tallies PASS/FAIL by inspecting each task's\n# logfile.txt.\n#\n# Usage: bash formal/run_all.sh [checks-cfg-path]\n#   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\n#   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\n#\n# Env vars (orchestrator-driven, override $1 and defaults):\n#   WRAPPER     — path to wrapper SV (default formal/wrapper.sv)\n#   CHECKS_CFG  — path to checks config (default formal/checks.cfg)\n# When BOTH are unset, the script auto-detects nret from\n# cores/$CORE_NAME/core.yaml: nret=1 routes to wrapper_si.sv +\n# checks_si.cfg; nret=2 (or absent) uses the defaults. Agents\n# invoking `bash formal/run_all.sh` directly therefore get the\n# right wrapper without needing to know the env-var plumbing.\nset -e\n\nif [ -z \"${RTL_DIR:-}\" ] || [ -z \"${CORE_NAME:-}\" ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: formal/run_all.sh requires RTL_DIR and CORE_NAME env vars.\" >&2\n  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl CORE_NAME=v1 bash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPROJECT_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$SCRIPT_DIR/..\" && pwd)\"\nRISCV_FORMAL=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/riscv-formal\"\n# Per-invocation work dir + log, unique among every process sharing this\n# riscv-formal checkout (the K concurrent agents of a run share it through\n# their worktrees' symlink). The name used to be \"$CORE_NAME-$$\", but an\n# agent's sandboxed shell runs in its own PID namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n# for every agent, so siblings wrote into one dir and wiped each other's\n# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n# FORMAL_WORK_ID pins the suffix so tools/eval/formal.py can remove exactly\n# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core\n…[7366 of 10438 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:bfda1904cb0b15e8]…\nStatus: PREUNSAT (rc=16). The property holds vacuously\n        # over the empty set of ch1-valid traces — a legitimate pass.\n        # Dual-issue hypotheses make the assumption satisfiable, so this\n        # branch never matches and the regular DONE (PASS branch covers it.\nlrwxrwxrwx+ 1 nobody nogroup 66 Nov 22 07:48 formal/riscv-formal -> /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep5/formal/riscv-formal\ntotal 56\ndrwxrwx---+  2 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 22 07:48 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody nogroup  4096 Nov 22 07:56 ..\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2630 Nov 22 07:48 checks-deep.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2658 Nov 22 07:48 checks.cfg\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  1455 Nov 22 07:48 checks_si.cfg\nlrwxrwxrwx+  1 nobody nogroup    66 Nov 22 07:48 riscv-formal -> /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep5/formal/riscv-formal\n-rwxrwx---+  1 nobody nogroup 10597 Nov 22 07:48 run_all.sh\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  4615 Nov 22 07:48 wrapper.sv\n-rw-rw----+  1 nobody nogroup  2863 Nov 22 07:48 wrapper_si.sv\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git status --short --untracked-files=all && git diff --check && cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-001-r8s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261122-001-r8s0\ntitle: Resolve branches with parallel operand comparisons\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The decoded-FIFO champion scores 216.99 CoreMark iterations/s at 86.362 MHz\n  over 3,979,945 marker cycles. Branch resolution runs from the forwarded\n  operands through a selection of full-width comparisons and into the\n  redirect that squashes younger issue. That feedback path constrained the\n  earlier registered recovery experiment and still appears among the long\n  paths in current layouts. Each of the six branch conditions can use the\n  same equality and ordered comparison hardware.\nhypothesis: |\n  In EX, compute equality and less-than for four eight-bit operand groups\n  in parallel. Flip both operand sign bits for signed ordering in the\n  highest group. Combine the less-than results by allowing each group to\n  decide only when all more significant groups are equal. Whole-word\n  equality is the AND of the same group-equality flags. Legal branch\n  funct3 bit 2 selects equality or ordering, bit 1 selects signedness\n  for ordering, and bit 0 inverts the predicate for BNE and BGE/BGEU.\n\n  Use the predicate at the existing EX decision edge for direction, RVFI\n  successor, and predictor training. Preserve the control-flow alignment\n  traps, recovery and FIFO flush, and stall qualification. Check the six\n  legal branch encodings against full-width comparisons, including signed\n  boundaries and operands that first differ across group boundaries.\n\n  The scratch implementation reached 80.967, 88.751, and 88.751 MHz.\n  At the champion's marker count the median projects to 223.00 iter/s\n  and leaves the divider as the limit in the median placements. That\n  result is 1.58 MHz below the roughly 90.34 MHz promotion hurdle. Treat\n  5% as a low-confidence target and remeasure the selected RTL across\n  all three placements with the unchanged correctness gates.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Replace the branch case of full-width comparisons with parallel eight-bit equality and less-than groups and the decoded branch predicate selection. Keep alignment, advance, redirect, training, and RVFI behavior.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
