{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_37", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '(liveness|run|checks)' formal/run_all.sh | head -35; sed -n '1,120p' formal/checks_si.cfg\"", "aggregated_output": "2:# Run riscv-formal checks against the current $RTL_DIR/*.sv.\n5:# Stages every $RTL_DIR/*.sv plus wrapper.sv + the chosen checks config under\n6:# the riscv-formal tree, then runs sby -> bitwuzla via the framework's\n10:# Usage: bash formal/run_all.sh [checks-cfg-path]\n11:#   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\n12:#   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\n16:#   CHECKS_CFG  — path to checks config (default formal/checks.cfg)\n19:# checks_si.cfg; nret=2 (or absent) uses the defaults. Agents\n20:# invoking `bash formal/run_all.sh` directly therefore get the\n25:  echo \"ERROR: formal/run_all.sh requires RTL_DIR and CORE_NAME env vars.\" >&2\n26:  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl CORE_NAME=v1 bash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\" >&2\n34:# riscv-formal checkout (the K concurrent agents of a run share it through\n36:# agent's sandboxed shell runs in its own PID namespace where $$ is 2 or 3\n38:# checks mid-SBY (V2 incident 03). mktemp gives a unique name instead.\n40:# its own dir afterwards. genchecks.py derives @core@ from the dir's\n41:# basename (genchecks.py:39), so @core@ = \"$CORE_NAME-<suffix>\".\n65:LOG=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/last_run-$WORK_ID.log\"\n67:# Hold a lock on the work dir for this run's lifetime. The reaper below\n79:# are both unset and $1 (checks-cfg-path) wasn't given either. Explicit\n98:        CHECKS_CFG=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/checks_si.cfg\"\n99:        echo \"[run_all.sh] auto-detected nret=1 from $CORE_YAML; using wrapper_si.sv + checks_si.cfg\"\n103:CHECKS_CFG=\"${CHECKS_CFG:-${1:-$SCRIPT_DIR/checks.cfg}}\"\n106:    echo \"ERROR: checks.cfg not found at $CHECKS_CFG\"\n127:# Reap work dirs (and their logs) left by runs that have ended: the lock\n131:# run_all.sh dozens of times.\n141:            rm -f \"$SCRIPT_DIR/last_run-${stale##*-}.log\"\n147:# Truncate the run log; genchecks + make are tee'd here in full.\n150:# Stage rtl + wrapper + the chosen checks config under the framework's\n151:# expected layout. genchecks.py looks for \"checks.cfg\" by name, so the\n156:# previous run, and genchecks/yosys silently picks up the old file\n163:# Stage checks.cfg with [verilog-files] auto-derived from actual rtl/\n164:# contents instead of the cfg's hardcoded list. The shipped checks.cfg\n170:STAGED_CFG=\"$CORE_DIR/checks.cfg\"\n185:# genchecks.py derives @core@ from the cwd's basename (genchecks.py:39),\n190:rm -rf checks/\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
