{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_22", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261122-003-r(8|9)s2\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(x[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\", x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"], \\\"\\\\n\\\", x[\\\"error\\\"], \\\"\\\\n\\\", x.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\")) for x in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-003-r8s2 \n {'motivation': 'The champion spends 3,979,945 cycles in the stalled CoreMark window.\\nA scratch trace found 65,243 redirects and more than 208,000 taken\\nconditional backedges spanning at most 16 words. A short-loop stream\\npredictor can use the gaps in imem readiness to keep feeding issue\\nwhile the current request sequence stays inside a trained loop.\\nA first replay prototype ran in 3,755,433 cycles with the canonical\\nCRCs, a 5.64% cycle reduction. Its 65.437 MHz Gowin median exposed a\\nserial replay lookup and request-PC mux that needs to be retimed.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Train one 16-word loop stream buffer from advancing, legal conditional\\nbranches that resolve taken to a lower, word-aligned PC, with both\\nPCs in the fetch aperture. Register the EX observation before checking\\nthe span. Keep the loop start and backedge as the descriptor. Clear\\nthe word-valid state when replacing it. Populate members from accepted\\nready responses and retain the decoded instruction and exact direct target. Index by\\nthe low four word-address bits. A loop can span two adjacent 16-word\\nblocks. Compare their upper address tags and use block-specific valid\\nbits so two PCs with the same index cannot be mistaken for one another.\\n\\nPrefer the live response on every ready cycle. During an imem stall,\\nreplay one valid member at the effective request PC if the issue FIFO\\ncan accept it. Recompute the applied direction and saved index using\\nthe current gshare state. A replayed branch resolves and trains through\\nthe normal EX path. A wrong successor on loop exit or another transfer\\nsquashes younger packets and immediately restores the resolved request.\\nClear the replay state on reset and on an accepted FENCE.I. Inhibit replay\\nand new loop training while any accepted FENCE.I awaits EX advance\\nor squash. Retain the last-word aperture guard and single retirement.\\n\\nRegister the live direct target and cached direct target in parallel\\nwith fall-through, retry, and the existing EX recovery address. Select\\n\n…[9046 of 12118 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b01c4f373fd55330]…\n1:49:37 [causal_ch0] summary: Elapsed clock time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:43:11 (2591)\nSBY 11:49:37 [causal_ch0] summary: Elapsed process time [H:MM:SS (secs)]: 0:00:00 (0)\nSBY 11:49:37 [causal_ch0] summary: engine_0 (smtbmc bitwuzla) did not return a status\nSBY 11:49:37 [causal_ch0] summary: engine_0 did not produce any traces\nSBY 11:49:37 [causal_ch0] DONE (ERROR, rc=16)\n\nFull run log: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-003-r9s2/formal/last_run-h001bf25a32df4f5.log\nPer-check logs in: /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-003-r9s2/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-h001bf25a32df4f5/checks/<check>/logfile.txt\n/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep5/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261122-003-r9s2/formal/run_all.sh: line 204: 1442714 Killed                     make -j\"$JOBS\" -k -f makefile 2>&1\n     1442715                          | tee -a \"$LOG\"\n     1442716                          | grep -E \"^(make|SBY|yosys|==|ERROR)\" \n \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
