{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nlines=[json.loads(line) for line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')]\nprint(lines[-1].keys())\nfor row in lines[-9:]:\n print('\\\\n',row['id'],row['title'])\n if row['id'].endswith(('r10s0','r10s1','r8s1','r9s1')):\n  for k,v in row.items():\n   if k not in ('id','title','category','changes'): print(k, str(v)[:6000])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "dict_keys(['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson'])\n\n hyp-20261122-001-r8s0 Resolve branches with parallel operand comparisons\n\n hyp-20261122-002-r8s1 Register fetch address candidates before steering\nmotivation The bench champion scores 216.99 iterations/s at a median 86.362 MHz over\n3,979,945 CoreMark marker cycles. Its reported 16.665 ns Gowin path starts\nat the synthetic instruction source and ends at the fetch request register.\nThe direct target goes through target arithmetic, the aperture check, and\nnext-PC selection before it reaches that register. A scratch implementation\nwith separate full-width registers for all four address candidates preserved\nthe marker count and reached 87.023 MHz median. Its critical path shifted\nto the divider. Scratch variants that merged replay with the sequential\nlane or retimed the FIFO squash scored lower. Keep the four distinct lanes\nand reduce the speculative target lane to the address bits it can use.\n\nhypothesis {'motivation': 'The bench champion scores 216.99 iterations/s at a median 86.362 MHz over\\n3,979,945 CoreMark marker cycles. Its reported 16.665 ns Gowin path starts\\nat the synthetic instruction source and ends at the fetch request register.\\nThe direct target goes through target arithmetic, the aperture check, and\\nnext-PC selection before it reaches that register. A scratch implementation\\nwith separate full-width registers for all four address candidates preserved\\nthe marker count and reached 87.023 MHz median. Its critical path shifted\\nto the divider. Scratch variants that merged replay with the sequential\\nlane or retimed the FIFO squash scored lower. Keep the four distinct lanes\\nand reduce the speculative \n…[32287 of 35359 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5fc513ad25e092d6]…\ndress. Options 1 and 2 were limited by the fetch recovery path into the next direct target. Gowin reported 4,761 logic cells and 1,148 registers, up from 4,224 and 954 for the champion.\n- Local formal was incomplete. The stock single-channel ALTOPS run generated 53 checks on the final RTL. Liveness, retirement uniqueness, backward PC consistency, and causality passed. The remaining checks had no result within the local budget. The run reported no counterexamples and required zero formal fix attempts.\n\ntimestamp 2026-11-22T12:43:03.593048Z\nslot 1\nround_id 10\nlesson - 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-002-r10s1 (improvement, +15.30%): A parallel MEM lane captures the ready operand in EX and uses the registered MEM/WB result to let load-to-branch and multiply-to-add pairs issue back-to-back, saving 2.81% of stalled CoreMark cycles, while shortening the divider and EX-to-data-address paths helped raise median Gowin Fmax from 84.107 to 96.774 MHz.\n\n hyp-20261122-003-r10s2 Read predicted loop words one cycle ahead of replay\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
