{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor row in map(json.loads, open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')):\n notes=row.get('implementation_notes') or ''\n if any(word in notes.lower() for word in ['branch density','retirement trace','split of the fetch','carry-select','jalr','slack','operand register']):\n  print(row['id'],row['title'],row.get('critical_path'))\n  for line in notes.splitlines():\n   if any(word in line.lower() for word in ['retirement trace','split of the fetch','carry-select','jalr']): print(line.strip()[:600])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 16-entry tagged branch target buffer {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -198.735, 'arrival_ns': 209.03, 'logic_cells': 151, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_fwd', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nEX trains on advancement. Eligible conditional branches store their direct target for either outcome and saturate their direction counter, starting at the corresponding weak state on replacement. Eligible JAL and JALR write a strongly taken entry with the resolved target. Training requires a legal control instruction and aligned source and target addresses within the instruction aperture.\n- `make test TARGET=bench` passed all 83 cocotb cases. Directed pipeline tests check direction reversals and saturation, one training update through a dmem hold, conflicting tags, changing JALR targets, recovery with both bus stalls, and stale predictions on a non-control instruction and a misaligned jump.\nhyp-20261122-003-r2s2 Fetch-time direct targets with a 64-entry gshare predictor {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_26_s0', 'slack_ns': -16.871, 'arrival_ns': 27.165, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nEX resolves direct transfers from the latched target and computes JALR from forwarded rs1 and the immediate. The resolved direction drives recovery, and the resolved successor feeds RVFI. A data-memory hold defers recovery and training. When EX advances, a redirect squashes ID/EX and takes priority over instruction-memory backpressure.\n- All 78 cocotb cases passed. Directed tests cover consecutive counter aliasing, reversals in both directions, stalled recovery, misaligned and reserved direct transfers, forwarded JALR, and the exact nine-cycle cold BEQ and eight-cycle predicted JAL divider retirement gaps.\nhyp-20261122-001-r5s0 Register operand data and bypass matches together in Decode {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0', 'to': 'dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s', 'slac\n…[3467 of 6539 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4eb9445c2ba3a92e]…\nneration, branch comparison, RV32M and RVFI source capture continue to consume the ordinary forwarded operands.\nThe pipeline tests cover immediate and register SLL, SRL and SRA on a negative operand at counts 0, 1, 16 and 31. They check forwarded register counts with populated upper bits, adjacent retirement, a held SRA followed by a queued SRL, JAL/JALR link consumers, and alignment traps that preserve the destination register.\nhyp-20261122-002-r9s1 Retain decoded packets behind a registered issue head {'from': 'lfsr_3_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/request_high_q_19_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.157, 'arrival_ns': 18.451, 'logic_cells': 27, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']}\n- The immediate/target field reduced the area of the packet RAM and head. A further split of the fetch target adder preserved the marker count and lowered the measured frequency, so the submitted RTL keeps the original target adder. Bitwuzla confirmed equality and signed and unsigned ordering for the submitted byte comparator over all 32-bit operands.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
