{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_56", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,110p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r11s1.yaml && rg -n 'TEST_DIR|RTL_DIR|runner|pytest' Makefile cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py | tail -n 25\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261122-002-r11s1\ntitle: Carry split direct targets across the fetch register\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The champion scores 250.19 CoreMark iterations/s at a 96.774 MHz Gowin\n  median over 3,868,036 marker cycles. The reproduced placement-1 setup\n  path starts at the registered EX recovery bit and ends at bit 25 of the\n  architectural direct target in ID/EX. It crosses the request PC mux,\n  the 18-bit sum and the upper-page adjustment. Moving carry correction\n  beyond the existing register boundaries removes those dependent steps\n  from the same cycle and keeps a predicted target available on schedule.\nhypothesis: |\n  Split the 18-bit in-aperture word sum at bit 8 of the byte address.\n  Compute the low six-bit sum and the zero-carry middle twelve-bit sum\n  independently. Precompute the middle increment toggle mask from prefix\n  ANDs of middle PC XOR middle displacement. An incoming carry flips\n  bit i precisely when the two operands are complementary below i.\n  Register both sums, the middle toggle mask and the low carry in the\n  predicted-address lane. In the request cycle, XOR the carry-qualified\n  mask into the middle sum in parallel with the other request lanes.\n  A taken prediction still requests its target on the next cycle.\n\n  For aperture qualification, combine middle generate with middle\n  propagate AND low carry. Check whether the upper PC plus this carry\n  minus the displacement sign is zero modulo 4096 using a truth table\n  over the upper PC being zero, one or all ones. Apply the existing\n  target alignment and gshare checks on the acceptance cycle. Carry\n  the split target and its adjustment metadata 