{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_65", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261122-003-r11s2\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys;d=json.load(sys.stdin);print(d[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]);print(d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\")[:9000])'\"", "aggregated_output": "Train a 64-entry loop stream buffer from resolved, taken conditional\nbackedges spanning at most 64 words. Latch the observation before\nchecking the span, alignment, and instruction aperture. Fill it from\naccepted ready instruction responses within the trained interval. Tag\neach word by its exact PC within the aperture and retain tags and\npayloads across interval changes. Include legal conditional branches\nand JAL whose targets are aligned and in the aperture. Store their\n18-bit target word. Use live fetch for the remaining direct transfers,\nJALR, FENCE.I, and the last aperture word.\n\nBank the entries by word parity and read the current and next\nsequential word in parallel. Register matching payloads before they\ncan enter the issue FIFO. Read from the registered sequential and\nretry candidates and qualify the staged hits by an actual hold or\nsequential advance. Discard hits that cross either recovery or a taken\nprediction. On an unavailable bus cycle, enqueue a staged hit at the\nFIFO tail if there is space. Keep ready responses and their empty-FIFO\nbypass on the live lane. A replayed direct transfer uses its saved\ntarget and the ordinary current-PC gshare decision and lookup index.\nEX or MEM resolves and trains it through the same path as a live branch.\n\nKeep live and replay steering separate up to their registered request\nselects. Capture the replay target in a separate narrow in-aperture\ncandidate, and use the existing sequential candidate for fall-through\nand the full-width retry candidate when neither lane advances. Form\nthe FIFO write-data selection at the tail. Use eight physical FIFO\nslots with four logical entries so the tail is always free for a\ntentative physical write. Only accepted traffic advances the pointer.\nStage the replay fill address and payload before the RAM write and\ninvalidate on reset and accepted FENCE.I. Kill pending fills and\ninhibit replay, fill and training until accepted fences advance or\nare squashed. Preserve MEM-before-EX recovery and single retirement.\n\nIn IF compute the live targ\n…[2803 of 5875 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:913642c73503dc89]…\nall 117 cocotb cases passed. Co-simulation used `NRET=1` to match the core manifest and covered four ELFs both ready and stalled. The CoreMark CRCs passed with 3,549,156 stalled marker cycles, down 8.24% from r10s1.\n- Local single-issue formal reached 52 of 53 passes within the agent budget. `reg_ch0` was still running at the final check. An intermediate run hit a Yosys parser error when `$bits` was applied to the replay entry type. Taking `$bits` of the packed entry signal fixed elaboration. The formal wrapper holds imem ready high. Cocotb and stalled ISS comparisons exercise replay.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` confirmed Gowin placements of 82.844, 87.041, and 87.041 MHz with distributed RAM for the replay banks and FIFO. The 87.041 MHz median gives 245.24 iterations per second, down 1.98% from r10s1 and below the promotion gate. Paths from registered fetch selects into the FIFO write data limited all three placements. The option 0 build used 5,757 logic cells, 1,552 registers, and 131 LUT-RAM units.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
