h step, append two input\\nbits to the current remainder, subtract D, 2D, and 3D in parallel with\\n35-bit borrow detection, and select the largest multiple that fits, or\\nzero. That choice yields the next two quotient bits and the new\\nremainder. Register the running remainder and quotient between cycles.\\nApply the quotient or remainder sign from the registered final state.\\nReturn the original dividend for remainder by zero and all ones for\\ndivision by zero. Preserve signed INT_MIN / -1 and its zero remainder.\\nKeep the same launch, wait, and acceptance schedule for edge cases an\n…[3205 of 6277 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:257d868575e85ff8]…\nross RV32M divide and remainder improvement \nhyp-20261122-002-r2s1 Retiming bypass selection across the decode-to-execute boundary regression \nhyp-20261122-002-r3s1 Move RV32M result completion to the memory stage improvement \nhyp-20261122-002-r4s1 Register divider operands before arithmetic setup improvement \nhyp-20261122-002-r5s1 Preselect all execute operands and isolate data address generation improvement \nhyp-20261122-002-r6s1 Split divider rounds by divisor magnitude improvement \nhyp-20261122-002-r7s1 Buffer decoded instructions ahead of register read and issue improvement \nhyp-20261122-002-r8s1 Register fetch address candidates before steering regression \nhyp-20261122-002-r9s1 Retain decoded packets behind a registered issue head regression \nhyp-20261122-002-r10s1 Execute late-result consumers in a parallel MEM lane improvement \nhyp-20261122-002-r11s1 Carry split direct targets across the fetch register regression \nhyp-20261122-002-r12s1 Pipeline the shifter through the MEM completion lane regression \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
