ads in MEM. Keep architectural reset\\nand the standalone register-file write-first mode. Use its raw read\\nmode in core so the captured WB source supplies write-first behavior.\\n\\nFeed a dedicated load/store address adder from the selected rs1 and\\nthe decoded I/S displacement. Sum the low 12 bits with carry out\\nand compute base[31:12] plus one and minus one in parallel.\\nIncrement the upper word for a nonnegative offset with carry and\\ndecrement it for a negative offset without carry. Pass the base\\nupper word through in the other cases. Capture the full modulo-2^32\\neffective byte address in EX/MEM. Use it for the data bus, lane\\nselection, alig\n…[42313 of 45385 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:45ccb31df2fb5e84]…\nhe other 48 checks remain unverified. The logs show solver waits and no counterexample, so no formal repair retries were made.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement option | Fmax (MHz) | Block RAMs | Worst setup path |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| 0 | 82.137 | 4 | ID/EX rs2 forwarding select through the ALU to EX/MEM result |\n| 1 | 90.676 | 4 | EX/MEM result through forwarding and the ALU back to EX/MEM result |\n| 2 | 90.676 | 4 | EX/MEM result through forwarding and the ALU back to EX/MEM result |\n\nThe 90.676 MHz median yields 234.42 CoreMark iterations/s, below the 101.23 MHz promotion threshold at this cycle count. Gowin reports 4,807 logic cells and 1,198 registers, an increase of 46 cells and 50 registers over the champion. The address-sum and upper-correction endpoints fall outside the 25 worst setup paths in each report. Option 0 also has MEM recovery into ID/EX within 0.003 ns of its limiting ALU path. Options 1 and 2 show divider remainder feedback and recovery within 0.031 ns of the limiting setup slack.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
