{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r8s1','r9s0','r9s1','r10s1','r11s1','r12s0')):\n  p=d.get('critical_path') or {}\n  print(d['id'], d['fmax_mhz'], d['cycles'], d['fitness'], {k:p.get(k) for k in ('from','to','logic_cells')})\n  notes=d.get('implementation_notes','')\n  print(notes[-3100:])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-002-r8s1 87.114 3979945 218.88 {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_5_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_13_s0', 'logic_cells': 12}\n# Register fetch address candidates before steering\n\nFetch captures the predicted target, sequential successor, replay address, and EX recovery address in parallel. The one-hot steering registers give EX recovery priority on the same edge that flushes the FIFO and squashes issue. The predicted lane holds 18 word-address bits. Fetch qualifies it with the full computed target and alignment, and the issue packet carries the full architectural target to EX. The sequential, replay, and recovery lanes each hold 30 word-address bits.\n\nEX shares the low 31-bit comparison between signed and unsigned branches. The operand sign bits resolve comparisons with differing signs, and the low bit of funct3 inverts complementary conditions. This change reduces logic on the branch resolution path feeding recovery. The fetch-only build reached 78.081 MHz median, with a redirect path limiting one placement and divider paths limiting the other two.\n\nThe directed pipeline tests cover a ready JAL blocked by a full FIFO, a redirect coincident with a younger taken prediction, replay of a stalled recovery target, and sequential release of the last-word hold. They check fetch addresses, retirement timing and order, and data-bus side effects. They also exercise signed and unsigned branch ordering for mixed-sign, same-sign, and equal operands.\n\nVerilator lint and all seven bench cocotb runners passed. Selftest and the three random programs matched the ISS with ready and stalled memory. Canonical stalled CoreMark passed the CRC and completion checks and took 3,979,945 marker cycles for 10 iterations.\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 83.351, 87.114, and 87.114 MHz. The 87.114 MHz median yields 218.88 iterations/s, below the 90.33 MHz promotion threshold at this marker count. The longest path in all three placements ends at the registered EX ALU result. For options 1 and 2, the redirect and d\n…[9302 of 12374 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:614bb67e43f8c902]…\nons 0, 1, and 2 reach 87.120, 96.774, and 96.774 MHz. The 96.774 MHz median clears the 87.793 MHz promotion threshold and scores 250.19 iterations/s, up 15.30% from 216.99. Option 0 was limited by EX forwarding into the data address. Options 1 and 2 were limited by the fetch recovery path into the next direct target. Gowin reported 4,761 logic cells and 1,148 registers, up from 4,224 and 954 for the champion.\n- Local formal was incomplete. The stock single-channel ALTOPS run generated 53 checks on the final RTL. Liveness, retirement uniqueness, backward PC consistency, and causality passed. The remaining checks had no result within the local budget. The run reported no counterexamples and required zero formal fix attempts.\n\nhyp-20261122-002-r11s1 94.169 3868036 243.45 {'from': 'cpu/u_if/write_ptr_q_1_s2', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.alu_select.sra_s0', 'logic_cells': 14}\n\nhyp-20261122-001-r12s0 94.983 3868036 245.56 {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_19_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.branch_cond_s0', 'logic_cells': 13}\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
