{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor d in map(json.loads,Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()):\n if d['id'] in ('hyp-20261122-002-r11s1','hyp-20261122-001-r13s0','hyp-20261122-001-r14s0'):\n  print(d['id'],d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][:3800],d['implementation_notes'][:2100])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-002-r11s1 Split the 18-bit in-aperture word sum between byte-address bits 7 and 8.\nCompute the low six-bit sum and the zero-carry middle twelve-bit sum\nindependently. Precompute the middle increment toggle mask from prefix\nANDs of middle PC XOR middle displacement. An incoming carry flips\nbit i precisely when the two operands are complementary below i.\nRegister both sums, the middle toggle mask and the low carry in the\npredicted-address lane. In the request cycle, XOR the carry-qualified\nmask into the middle sum in parallel with the other request lanes.\nA taken prediction still requests its target on the next cycle.\n\nFor aperture qualification, combine middle generate with middle\npropagate AND low carry. Check whether the upper PC plus this carry\nminus the displacement sign is zero modulo 4096 using a truth table\nover the upper PC being zero, one or all ones. Apply the existing\ntarget alignment and gshare checks on the acceptance cycle. Carry\nthe split target and its adjustment metadata through the FIFO and\nID/EX, and form the full architectural target in EX in parallel with\nbranch comparison. This includes the original target alignment bit and\nall 32 address bits for RVFI and redirect. Preserve older MEM recovery\npriority, the last-word aperture hold and the late branch lane.\n\nA bit-vector check proved the split sum and aperture test equivalent to\nfull-width addition. The six-bit scratch split passed the ISA traces\nand completed CRC-validated CoreMark in 3,868,036 marker cycles. Its\nGowin timings were 88.375, 94.328 and 94.328 MHz, yielding 243.87\niterations/s. EX forwarding into the ALU set the median, with the divider\nrecurrence close behind. Promotion needs a median above 101.23 MHz at\nthis cycle count. The 103 MHz target, about 266 iterations/s, depends on\nclearing those placement limits. Run all three placements and the stock\nsingle-retire formal, cosim and stalled CoreMark gates on implementation.\n \nhyp-20261122-001-r13s0 Form the normal request word from the registered sequential, predicted,\n\n…[4650 of 7722 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:19c604367506ef1c]…\nequests still launch from the registered address, with the existing stall and recovery controls.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint and all 115 cocotb cases passed. The added coverage includes both forwarding ports, signed immediate wraparound, mixed ALU and ADDI producer priority, EX and MEM squash, store backpressure, and late ADDI completion with a writing or trapping predecessor.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed for selftest and three random programs, each on both ready and stalled buses, plus canonical stalled CoreMark. CoreMark validated in 3,868,036 marker cycles with no out-of-bounds access.\n- A five-cycle bounded SAT check of the issue, EX and MEM datapath passed for symbolic operand values, displacements, tags, producer choices, late matches, issue bubbles, and holds. It compared the captured address and writeback sum to full-width arithmetic and checked both reported operand values.\n- The stock `formal/run_all.sh` selected the single-retire wrapper and ALTOPS configuration. It tim\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c '\"$TMPDIR/r15-profile/obj/cosim_sim\" \"$TMPDIR/r15-profile/coremark.elf\" 10000000 --bench --istall --dstall\n\"$TMPDIR/r15-profile/obj/cosim_sim\" \"$TMPDIR/r15-profile/coremark.elf\" 10000000 --istall --dstall | python3 -c '\"'\nimport collections,json,sys\nnames={0x3:\\\"load\\\",0x23:\\\"store\\\",0x33:\\\"op\\\",0x13:\\\"imm\\\",0x63:\\\"branch\\\",0x67:\\\"jalr\\\",0x6f:\\\"jal\\\",0x37:\\\"lui\\\",0x17:\\\"auipc\\\"}\nclasses=collections.Counter()\nlate=collections.Counter()\ntransfers=collections.Counter()\nprev=None\nactive=False\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(line)\n instr=d.get(\\\"insn\\\",0)\n if d.get(\\\"mem_wmask\\\") and d[\\\"mem_addr\\\"]==0x10000100: active=True; continue\n if not active: continue\n if d.get(\\\"mem_wmask\\\") and d[\\\"mem_addr\\\"]==0x10000104: break\n op=instr&127; f3=(instr>>12)&7; f7=instr>>25\n cat=(\\\"mul\\\" if instr&0xfe00007f==0x02000033 and f3<4 else names.get(op,hex(op)))\n classes[cat]+=1\n if cat in (\\\"branch\\\",\\\"jalr\\\",\\\"jal\\\"): transfers[cat,d[\\\"pc_wdata\\\"]\"'!=d[\"pc_rdata\"]+4]+=1\n if prev and prev[0] in (\"load\",\"mul\") and prev[1]:\n  match1=prev[1]==d[\"rs1_addr\"]; match2=prev[1]==d[\"rs2_addr\"]\n  if match1 or match2:\n   uses1=op in (3,0x23,0x33,0x13,0x63,0x67); uses2=op in (0x23,0x33,0x63)\n   late[prev[0],cat,f3 if cat in (\"branch\",\"op\",\"imm\") else None,\"both\" if match1 and uses1 and match2 and uses2 else \"rs1\" if match1 and uses1 else \"rs2\" if match2 and uses2 else \"unused\"]+=1\n prev=(cat,d[\"rd_addr\"])\nprint(classes); print(transfers)\nfor k,v in late.most_common(): print(k,v)'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
