{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_42", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nentries=map(json.loads,Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines())\nfor d in entries:\n if d['id'] in ('hyp-20261122-002-r9s1', 'hyp-20261122-003-r14s2'):\n  print(d['id']); print(d['hypothesis']['hypothesis'][:4200]); print(d['implementation_notes'][:7500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-002-r9s1\nUse 32 direct-mapped slots indexed by the word PC to hold decoded issue\npackets, with exact remaining PC tags and separate reuse-valid bits.\nKeep four FIFO reference entries. A live accepted word writes its\ndecoded packet into the indexed slot and queues that slot number. A\nreferenced slot is pinned until its last outstanding reference drains.\nOn a ready response that aliases a pinned slot, hold the request and\nlet the FIFO drain in order. On an imem stall, accept a stored packet\nonly on an exact valid tag match. Limit reuse to fall-through words\naway from the last word of the instruction aperture, so reuse advances\nby PC+4 and conditional and indirect transfers still use live fetch.\n\nRegister the oldest queued payload at the issue boundary. Read the\nsecond reference ahead of a possible pop and replace the head on the\npop edge. When a new arrival becomes the head, take the live decoded\nresponse or the payload at the request slot. Preserve empty-queue\nflow-through for a ready live response and register a reused packet\nbefore issue. Keep the two five-bit source tags with each reference\nand the registered head so the hazard and register-file read paths\nstart from fabric flops. Keep a narrow indexed copy for reused source\ntags and advance it with the same acceptance as the payload.\n\nTrack the four reference-valid bits separately from packet reuse\nvalidity. Use the registered redirect to make old references\nimmediately invisible at the corrected request and rebase the queue\non that cycle. Speculative reference and head captures can use the\nissue candidate before the kill decision. Keep the existing same-edge\nsquash of ID/EX validity, with the corrected ready word eligible for\nimmediate issue. Preserve the last-word guard and the original\npredictor and single-channel retirement behavior.\n\nInvalidate reuse on reset and on acceptance of FENCE.I. Pause fetch\nafter accepting FENCE.I until that specific packet advances in EX or\nis squashed. Keep pinned payloads readable after invalidation so older\nword\n…[6665 of 9737 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8d056ce47891faca]…\nts immediately and keep replay and new fills disabled\nthrough the scrub. Preserve already queued payloads.\nBlock replay and fills until accepted fences advance or are\nsquashed, including fence accounting on the corrected request.\n\nA scratch prototype with branch-trained admission passed the\ncanonical CoreMark CRCs at 3,407,072 stalled marker cycles, an\n11.92% reduction. At that cycle count promotion needs a Gowin\nmedian above 89.163 MHz. A 90.5 MHz median would yield 265.62\niterations/s, a projected 6.17% gain. The single-read prototype\nreached 73.283 MHz. Its median setup path went from the resident\nRAM through issue hazard logic back to the next resident RAM read\naddress. A separate run also exposed the indexed validity bitmap\nwrite as a timing limit. Speculative parallel reads and in-RAM\nvalidity target those paths. Measure their timing and cycle impact.\nCheck all Gowin placements, stalled ISS traces, the canonical\nCoreMark CRCs and the existing single-retire formal checks,\nincluding the ready-bus retire\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
