{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_18", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,165p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-002-r1s1.yaml; sed -n '18,85p' tools/eval/gowin.py\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261122-002-r1s1\ntitle: Share a multicycle divider across RV32M divide and remainder\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The bench baseline runs at 5.442 MHz. Its 199.837 ns worst path spans\n  forwarding and the execute ALU before reaching the data-memory path.\n  The signed and unsigned division and remainder operators are the likeliest\n  source of that depth. Their combinational results share the execute result\n  mux with ordinary ALU operations and memory addresses. Moving division to\n  a registered unit should shorten the clock period for every instruction.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use one blocking, registered divider for DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU. On\n  issue, capture forwarded operands and form unsigned magnitudes. Consume\n  a zero-padded 36-bit dividend in six cycles, six bits per cycle using\n  three radix-4 restoring steps. In each step, compute trial remainders\n  for one, two, and three times the divisor in parallel and pick the\n  largest non-borrowing subtraction. Register the running remainder and\n  quotient between cycles. Apply the quotient or remainder sign after the\n  last registered step and return the original dividend for remainder by\n  zero or all ones for division by zero. Check signed INT_MIN / -1 and its\n  zero remainder explicitly. Keep all DIV/REM operations on the same\n  schedule in RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS with the existing four substitute results.\n\n  Launch only when the divide is valid in EX and the older EX/MEM entry\n  can advance. Hold fetch and ID/EX from launch through the six steps.\n  During that interval, feed bubbles into EX/MEM as any older memory and\n  writeback work drains. Capture the forwarded source values at launch\n  for retirement, since their producers can drain before completion.\n  The divide advances through EX/MEM on the following edge and publishes\n  its result through normal forwarding and channel-0 retirement. Release\n  the front end on that acceptance edge so an immediate consumer sees the\n  result by EX bypass. Give an older stalled data request priority and\n  clear di\n…[3666 of 6738 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b78832339928ff8f]…\np_module core_bench\",\n        \"set_option -verilog_std sysv2017\",\n        \"set_option -output_base_name core_bench\",\n        f\"set_option -place_option {place_option}\",\n        \"set_option -gen_text_timing_rpt 1\",\n        \"run all\",\n        \"\",\n    ])\n\n\n_MAXF = re.compile(r\"^\\s*\\d+\\s+\\S+\\s+[\\d.]+\\(MHz\\)\\s+([\\d.]+)\\(MHz\\)\\s+(\\d+)\", re.M)\n\n\ndef _cells(rpt: str, name: str) -> int | None:\n    m = re.search(rf\"^\\s*{re.escape(name)}\\s*\\|\\s*(\\d+)\", rpt, re.M)\n    return int(m.group(1)) if m else None\n\n\ndef critical_paths(tr_text: str, n: int = 5) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"The n worst setup paths: endpoints, delay, logic cells and the\n    modules the path crosses (in order), from Gowin's timing report.\"\"\"\n    # The headings also appear, indented, in the report's table of contents.\n    m = re.search(r\"^3\\.3\\.1 Setup Analysis Report\", tr_text, re.M)\n    if not m:\n        return []\n    sec = tr_text[m.end():]\n    h = re.search(r\"^3\\.3\\.2 Hold Analysis Report\", sec, re.M)\n    sec = sec[:h.start()] if h else sec\n    out = []\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
