{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'structural|multipli|dsp|retim|critical.path' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; [print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in json.loads(l).items() if k not in (\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"notes\\\",\\\"timing\\\",\\\"result\\\",\\\"eval_result\\\")} )[:2500]) for l in sys.stdin]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-00eedbd\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T02:36:30.621996Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Fold DIV and REM into a shared radix-4 unit\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches 5.442 MHz and its 199.837 ns worst path traverses\\nforwarding and the EX ALU across 156 logic cells. The signed and unsigned\\ncombinational divide and remainder operators are the strongest candidate\\nfor that depth. Sharing and registering the division recurrence should\\nraise the clock rate for every instruction, with a direct cycle cost\\nconfined to DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU. A baseline Verilator run with both\\nstall streams reproduced all canonical CoreMark CRCs and the 4,491,485\\ncycles between markers. Its 2,922,015 retirements inside that window\\ncontained zero divide or remainder instructions.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 50, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/alu.sv\", \"description\": \"Remove the combinational divide and remainder datapaths. Preserve the other ALU operations.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/divrem_unit.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the clocked shared divider with launch, result-valid, and accept signals. Reset clears any outstanding operation. Preserve the four exact ALTOPS substitutions and release their results on the same schedule as hardwar\n…[4903 of 7975 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d63a1f0ebbca8e63]…\nme\": \"regression\", \"fitness\": 12.6, \"delta_pct\": 3.96, \"vs_baseline\": 3.96, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.334, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4234052, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12665, \"ff\": 509, \"seeds\": [4.908, 5.334, 5.334], \"perturbations\": [[0, 4.908, 146], [1, 5.334, 151], [2, 5.334, 151]], \"lutram\": 21, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -198.735, \"arrival_ns\": 209.03, \"logic_cells\": 151, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 146, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T02:58:44.049874Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 1, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r1s2 (regression, +3.96%): A fetch-local 16-entry tagged BTB saved 5.73% of CoreMark cycles by avoiding redirect bubbles on correct predictions, with the EX ALU still on the critical path and a drop in median post-placement Fmax from 5.442 to 5.334 MHz limiting the throughput gain.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
