with carry out\n  and compute base[31:12] plus one and minus one in parallel.\n  Increment the upper word for a nonnegative offset with carry and\n  decrement it for a negative offset without carry. Pass the base\n  upper word through in the other cases. Capture the full modulo-2\n…[2275 of 5347 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f6c9648fb353f8a6]…\n    description: Drive the raw fetched instruction and use packet validity to qualify acceptance during an imem stall.\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: Latch the one-hot selections with the operand payload. Clear ID/EX validity on redirect or bubble and hold payload and selections during an older stage hold.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Export fast-writer eligibility after trap checks and combine operands with the registered one-hot masks. Capture the dedicated address from forwarded rs1 and the signed I/S offset.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: Use the dedicated effective address for the bus, lane masks, alignment, load extraction and aligned RVFI address. Export the next MEM/WB write qualification after alignment checks.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check youngest-writer priority across all three bypass sources, capture of a WB collision across a stalled older store, fallback past trapping writers, and signed offsets crossing 4 KiB in both directions.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
