{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' tools/eval/_slots.py; ls -l /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh; rg -n 'GOWIN|LICENSE' setup.sh\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Host-wide slots for the harness's heavy evals (formal, Gowin builds).\n\nThree concurrent runs, each evaluating up to three slots, plus the agents'\nown self-checks, saturated the 20-core run host (load 20); formal checks then\nhit their wall-clock ceiling because of what other runs were doing, not\nbecause of the design (V2.1 campaign, first batch). With HARNESS_EVAL_SLOTS\nset, each eval holds one of that many flock'ed slots (in HARNESS_EVAL_LOCK_DIR,\noperator-only) for its duration, and its timeout starts once it holds one.\nUnset (agents' own `make timing`, tests): no limit. The variables use a prefix\nthe agent environment does not inherit (tools/agents/_runtime.py).\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport contextlib\nimport fcntl\nimport os\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\n@contextlib.contextmanager\ndef eval_slot(what: str = \"eval\"):\n    n = int(os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_SLOTS\", \"0\") or 0)\n    lock_dir = os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_LOCK_DIR\", \"\")\n    if n <= 0 or not lock_dir:\n        yield\n        return\n    d = Path(lock_dir)\n    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    started, told = time.time(), False\n    while True:\n        for i in range(n):\n            f = open(d / f\"slot{i}.lock\", \"w\")\n            try:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)\n            except BlockingIOError:\n                f.close()\n                continue\n            waited = time.time() - started\n            if waited > 60:\n                print(f\"  [eval] {what}: got host eval slot {i} after {waited:.0f}s\", flush=True)\n            try:\n                yield\n            finally:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n                f.close()\n            return\n        if not told:\n            print(f\"  [eval] {what}: waiting for a host eval slot ({n} busy)\", flush=True)\n            told = True\n        time.sleep(5)\n\n\ndef eval_jobs(default: str | None = None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"make -j for a formal run holding a slot (HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS).\"\"\"\n    return os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS\") or default\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 nobody nogroup 24968 Jul 10  2025 /opt/gowin/IDE/bin/gw_sh\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n e=json.loads(line)\n if e['id'].endswith('r5s1'):\n  print(e['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n e=json.loads(line)\n if e['id'].endswith('r5s1'):\n  print(e['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# Bench execute operand selection and data addresses\n\nDecode compares both encoded source tags with the eligible writers in EX, MEM, and WB. ID/EX captures four one-hot selects per operand and one shared snapshot of the writing WB stage's value alongside the raw register-file reads. EX uses a masked OR to select each operand. The register file retains synchronous reset and defaults to write-first operation for standalone callers. In core, raw-read mode lets the EX mux handle WB collisions and x0.\n\nThe existing forwarding module now computes the decode-stage selects. EX derives its fast-write qualification from legal decoder write control and the jump alignment check. MEM adds data alignment to its write qualification. Fetch carries the raw word with separate validity. ID/EX payload capture follows the decode hold, and reset, redirects, and late-result bubbles clear validity. During a data stall, MEM/WB retains the selected bypass value after clearing retirement validity. EX/MEM keeps the store address and data until acceptance. The divider retains its launch snapshots and handoff schedule.\n\nThe load/store adder sums the low 12 bits and computes upper increment and decrement candidates in parallel. The offset sign prepares the two possible upper words, and the low carry selects the final word. EX/MEM registers the modulo-2^32 byte address independently of the integer and link result. MEM uses the byte address for bus requests, alignment, lane selection, and the aligned RVFI address.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks on the final RTL without retries. The script used the existing single-channel wrapper and check configuration.\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All 94 cocotb cases passed, including competing writers on both operands, a WB collision held across a stalled store, trapping and squashed writers, an unready raw fetch, and signed I/S displacement boundaries.\n- Full RVFI co-simulation passed for selftest and all three random programs with ready buses and with both stall streams. Canonical stalled CoreMark passed the UART validation and all five CRC checks with no out-of-bounds accesses. Ten iterations took 4,233,123 marker cycles.\n- Gowin placements 0, 1, and 2 measured 73.504, 77.218, and 77.218 MHz. Placement 0 used 3,237 logic cells and 762 registers. The median yields 182.41 iterations/s, 24.82% above the champion. The divider recurrence limits all three placements. The measured median is 0.389 MHz below the prototype and 12.508 MHz above the tournament threshold.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The YAML passes schema validation. Every Gowin placement of the champion was divider-limited, so I’ll use a scratch prototype to check whether the parallel trial bank can clear the 80.77 MHz acceptance threshold."}}
