{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git show c540e83:cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c \\\"import json,sys; [print(d.get('hypothesis','')) for d in map(json.loads,sys.stdin) if d['id'].endswith('r4s0')]\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git show c540e83:cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c \\\"import json,sys; [print(d.get('hypothesis','')) for d in map(json.loads,sys.stdin) if d['id'].endswith('r4s0')]\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"{'motivation': \"The 129.62 iter/s champion reaches a 54.869 MHz Gowin median. Its\\nworst setup paths reach the divider's initial remainder through EX\\noperand selection and two dependent leading-nibble trials. The leading\\nquotient and remainder depend on just two four-bit values when the\\ndivisor magnitude is below 16. Collapsing the launch calculation can\\nraise the clock for every instruction, including the divide-free\\nCoreMark marker window.\\n\", 'hypothesis': \"Replace the two serial narrow radix-4 steps on launch with a\\ncombinational lookup for the four-bit prefix quotient and remainder.\\nLet A be the high nibble of the dividend magnitude and D be the low\\nnibble of the divisor magnitude. Use a one-hot decode of D to select\\namong 16 rows. In each row, the eight output bits are 16-bit truth\\ntable constants indexed by A. Store the quotient in the high four\\nbits and the remainder in the low four bits, then OR the masked rows.\\nFor positive D the row encodes A divided by D and A modulo D.\\nThe D=0 row gives quotient 15 and remainder A. Use\\nthe existing small-divisor test on raw operands to enable the lookup\\nonly for full divisor magnitudes below 16. Otherwise initialize with\\nquotient zero and remainder A.\\n\\nForm the launch magnitudes in parallel slices at bit boundaries\\n0, 8, 16, 24, 28, and 32. For a negative operand each slice is\\ncomplemented and incremented only if all lower raw operand bits\\nare zero. This exposes the high dividend nibble and low divisor\\nnibble to the lookup with short local carry chains. On the launch\\nedge, register the resulting prefix remainder, the 28 unconsumed\\ndividend bits concatenated with the prefix quotient, and the same\\nfull-width divisor multiples.\\n\\nKeep the two full-width radix-4 steps per work cycle and the\\nlaunch-plus-seven-work-edge schedule. Preserve held completion,\\nfinal-edge handoff to MEM, captured RVFI operands, and the exact\\nALTOPS substitutions. Exercise signed slice carries and divisor\\nboundaries, including division by zero and INT_MIN divided by -1.\\n\\nA SAT check proved that the prototype and champion initialize all\\ndivider state identically for every operand pair and operation code.\\nThe prototype passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS formal checks,\\nseven cocotb suites and five co-simulation ELFs. It passed the\\ncanonical stalled CoreMark CRC gate at\\n4,233,123 marker cycles for ten iterations, matching the champion.\\nIt measured 56.788, 59.483 and 59.483 MHz across\\nthe three vendor placements, shifting the median placement's worst\\npath to the integer EX-to-dmem path. The median yields 140.52 iter/s,\\n8.41% above the champion. The 4.6% acceptance margin requires about\\n57.394 MHz at this cycle count.\\nRecheck timing, formal, co-simulation and canonical stalled CoreMark\\non the tournament implementation.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 8, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/divider.sv', 'description': 'Replace the narrow launch trials with the row-decoded prefix table and chunk the magnitude conversion feeding launch. Preserve the full-width work recurrence, handoff, sign correction and ALTOPS branch.'}, {'file': 'test/test_divider.py', 'description': 'Extend the existing prefix vectors with negative operands immediately around the magnitude slice boundaries. Retain the existing exhaustive nibble, zero-divisor, exact-latency and held-completion checks.'}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
