selection.'}, {'file': 'rtl/alu.sv', 'description': 'Remove the four divide and remainder result arms and their arithmetic from the combinational ALU. Preserve RV32I operations and all four multiply operations.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Issue DIV/REM from valid ID/EX using forwarded operands, preserve retirement operands across the hold, and inject invalid side-effect-free EX/MEM bubbles until the divide result is ready. Publish the completed result with its original destination and instruction metadata.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Wire the divide interlock between EX and hazard control and retain the existing single-channel RVFI and memory handshakes.'}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Hold the PC and ID/EX on divide launch and during computation while allowing older stages to drain. Preserve the data-memory stall priority and existing load-use and r\n…[40138 of 43210 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b3d0170ea59cb4eb]…\n final-edge EX/MEM\\nacceptance, pending result, reset, and ALTOPS formulas and timing.\\n\\nKeep ID/EX operand outputs in fabric flip-flops by using two 16-word\\nasynchronous LUT-RAM register-file banks. Mask bank reads in\\nparallel with a resettable written bitmap. Preserve x0, standalone\\nwrite-first behavior, and the core's registered one-hot WB collision\\nselection. The bitmap suppresses stale bank contents after reset.\\n\\nA scratch prototype measured 77.281, 82.575, and 82.575 MHz across\\nthe three Gowin placements with 3,868 logic cells. Canonical stalled\\nCoreMark passed CRC validation in 4,233,123 marker cycles. The median\\nclock and measured cycle count give 195.07 iterations/s, 6.9 percent\\nabove the champion. Seven cocotb suites and five co-simulation ELFs\\npassed. The identical ALTOPS build passed all 53 formal checks,\\nincluding liveness. Acceptance requires a median above about 80.77 MHz\\nat this cycle count. Recheck timing and the existing correctness gates\\non the tournament implementation.\\n\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
