{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261122-(002-r6s1|003-r6s2|003-r5s2)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c '\nimport json,sys\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(l)\n print(d[\\\"id\\\"], d.get(\\\"critical_path\\\"), d.get(\\\"seeds\\\"))\n print(d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\"))\n'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-003-r5s2 {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -11.368, 'arrival_ns': 21.662, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']} [61.096, 64.667, 64.667]\n# Registered branch recovery\n\nEX forms a single alternate word address from the saved prediction or the forwarded JALR sum. IF registers that address every cycle alongside separate direction-miss and aperture-resume bits. The registered recovery state selects the imem and gshare request, masks the younger ID/EX packet, and presents the response directly to decode. On the next edge, IF rebases the queue and advances from an accepted response or retains the recovery PC for retry. RVFI continues to report the full resolved successor, and each advancing conditional branch trains its saved gshare index once.\n\nThe four-entry FIFO uses an asynchronous-read, synchronous-write packed-vector array. Its registered head and tail pointers determine physical write eligibility. A full queue resumes accepting responses on the cycle after a pop. Decode can drain the queue during imem backpressure, and fetch can fill it during dmem and divide holds. The last imem word issues through the empty bypass and waits for EX if its prediction is sequential.\n\nThe implementation also uses one-hot EX forwarding selects with the existing producer priority. The registered-recovery design with the original forwarding mux measured 60.380 MHz median. The one-hot mux raised the median above the 60.84 MHz hurdle. The longest paths still run from the register file through the EX ALU to dmem.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All 87 cocotb cases passed, including 27 pipeline cases. Coverage includes full-queue behavior, stalled training and recovery, wrong-path store and divide discard, aperture-edge retry and resume, and the existing exact divider and retirement-order checks.\n- The final RTL passed all 53 single-issue ALTOPS checks with `formal/run_all.sh`. The first \n…[2626 of 5698 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0c437b28c83fc871]…\nretirement interface.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed.\n- All 104 cocotb cases passed, including FIFO wraparound, stalled fetch and recovery, wrong-path store, load, and divide discard, aperture-edge requests, and the 9- and 10-cycle divider gaps.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed all eight RVFI trace comparisons, covering four ELFs in both bus modes. Stalled CoreMark completed 10 iterations in 3,979,945 marker cycles with canonical CRCs and no out-of-bounds accesses.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` scored 192.74 CoreMark iterations/s, 5.66% above the 182.41 iterations/s champion. Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 77.565, 76.709, and 76.709 MHz, respectively. Option 0 used 3,585 logic cells, 805 registers, and 33 LUT-RAM cells.\n- `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-issue ALTOPS checks on the final RTL.\n\nThe divider recurrence sets the median clock limit. The measured median clears the 75.938 MHz acceptance threshold by 0.771 MHz.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
