{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'\nfor line in open(p):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'] not in ('hyp-20261122-002-r7s1','hyp-20261122-001-r7s0','hyp-20261122-003-r7s2'): continue\n print(d['id'], list(d))\n for k,v in d.items():\n  if k in ('changes',): continue\n  if isinstance(v,dict): print(k,list(v))\n  else: print(k,str(v)[:5500])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-001-r7s0 ['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\nid hyp-20261122-001-r7s0\ntitle Register the preselected recovery address beside the fetch PC\ncategory micro_opt\nmotivation The 201.60 iter/s champion runs at an 85.341 MHz Gowin median over\n4,233,123 CoreMark marker cycles. A repeat of placement 0 showed that\nthe EX branch condition path to the fetch PC is within 0.003 ns of the\nreported EX ALU critical path. The condition selects the resolved PC\nand then drives fetch recovery arbitration. The direction and word\naddress needed for recovery can be prepared separately.\n\nhypothesis ['motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes']\nexpected_impact ['fitness_delta_pct', 'confidence']\noutcome regression\nfitness 206.22\ndelta_pct 2.29\nvs_baseline 1601.49\nfmax_mhz 87.297\nipc_coremark 2e-06\ncycles 4233123\niterations 10\nlut4 3969\nff 942\nseeds [83.541, 87.297, 87.297]\nperturbations [[0, 83.541, 14], [1, 87.297, 10], [2, 87.297, 10]]\nlutram 32\nbsram 4\ndsp 3\ncritical_path ['from', 'to', 'slack_ns', 'arrival_ns', 'logic_cells', 'modules']\nlogic_levels 14\nformal_passed True\ncosim_passed True\nerror None\nimplementation_notes # Registered fetch recovery\n\nID/EX captures the alternate direct successor with the applied prediction. A predicted-taken transfer saves PC+4, and a predicted-not-taken transfer saves the direct target. IF computes the fallthrough word once and supplies it to ID. EX still resolves the architectural next PC and applies alignment and link-write checks. The advancing miss pulse drives the existing same-edge ID/EX squash and qualifies capture of either the saved direct successor or the forwarded JALR target.\n\nThe registered miss pulse selects th\n…[11080 of 14152 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8d1c119f43d256ea]…\nran from scratch copies to keep generated files out of the protected directories and shared formal checkout.\n- `NRET=1 make fpga TARGET=bench` measured 211.54 CoreMark iterations/s over 3,979,945 marker cycles, a 4.93% gain over 201.60 iterations/s. The three Gowin placements reached 76.603, 84.192, and 84.192 MHz. Placement option 0 used 4,174 logic cells, 950 registers, and 51 LUT-RAM cells, 19 more LUT-RAM cells than the champion.\n- A split fetch-adder variant reached 216.53 iterations/s. Its register-consistency proof was still running without a counterexample near the deadline, so the delivered RTL uses the fully verified full-width adder.\n\ntimestamp 2026-11-22T06:17:06.923094Z\nslot 2\nround_id 7\nlesson - 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r7s2 (regression, +4.93%): Compressing the four-entry gshare FIFO to 73 bits with adder-free target reconstruction preserved the 5.98% stalled CoreMark cycle savings, with divider and ALU timing limiting Gowin Fmax to 84.192 MHz median and 76.603 MHz in the slowest placement.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
