n, with a direct cycle cost\\nconfined to DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU. A baseline Verilator run with both\\nstall streams reproduced all canonical CoreMark CRCs and the 4,491,485\\ncycles between markers. Its 2,922,015 retirements inside that window\\ncontained zero divide or remainder instructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline reaches 5.442 MHz and its 199.837 ns worst path traverses\\nforwarding and the EX ALU across 156 logic cells. The signed and unsigned\\ncom\n…[227405 of 230477 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6e408ce7bb9df146]…\n94 MHz fell short of the 85.238 MHz promotion target. The slowest paths reach the issue-valid register and the FIFO pointer resets through recovery and issue control.\\n- The first formal invocation stopped in Yosys parsing at the loop RAM width declaration. Applying `$bits` to a declared signal, as the existing FIFO does, resolved the error. The full suite remained incomplete within the local time budget. The causal, cover, illegal-instruction, liveness, backward-PC, and unique-order checks passed. The run produced no counterexample in the completed checks.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-22T08:42:03.768218Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-22 hyp-20261122-003-r8s2 (regression, -0.73%): Replaying decoded loop words into the flow-through issue FIFO during imem stalls saved 5.64% of stalled CoreMark cycles, with same-cycle EX recovery and issue control paths to ID/EX valid and the FIFO pointer resets limiting the retimed design to 80.894 MHz median Gowin Fmax against an 85.238 MHz promotion target.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
