{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_17", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json; rows=list(map(json.loads,sys.stdin)); [print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"motivation\\\"],sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for r in rows[-5:]]' && ls -l /srv/hwebench/tmp/7c172beb/a589e53d/bench-structural.uNuQOA/obj/cosim_sim\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-002-r4s1\nRegister divider operands before arithmetic setup\nThe champion scores 129.62 CoreMark iterations/s at a 54.869 MHz Gowin\nmedian and 4,233,123 marker cycles. Its worst reported setup path starts\nat a MEM/WB destination tag, crosses operand forwarding, and ends at\nthe divider's launch remainder register after 22 cells and 24.117 ns.\nEarlier measurements found no DIV/REM in the CoreMark marker window,\nso this launch path can limit the benchmark clock without doing useful\nwork in that window. The current nine-cycle retirement gap after a\nredirect or late-result bubble leaves one cycle within the existing\nready-bus formal liveness bound.\n\nhyp-20261122-002-r5s1\nPreselect all execute operands and isolate data address generation\nThe bench champion scores 146.14 CoreMark iterations/s at 61.864 MHz\nover 4,233,123 marker cycles. Its worst Gowin path starts at the\ninferred register-file block RAM and reaches data memory through\nthe register-file write-first mux, EX bypass, the integer ALU and\nthe jump-link mux. Prior decode-stage tag matching left the write-first\ndata mux in series with EX bypass. A load or store needs only the\nselected rs1 plus a signed 12-bit displacement.\n\nhyp-20261122-002-r6s1\nSplit divider rounds by divisor magnitude\nThe champion scores 182.41 CoreMark iterations/s at a 77.218 MHz Gowin\nmedian over 4,233,123 marker cycles. Its critical path in all three\nplacements crosses two dependent full-width radix-4 divider steps.\nEarlier traces found no DIV/REM inside the marker window, but every\ninstruction pays for the divider's clock period. A scratch redesign\nshortened the divider path and exposed a register-file block RAM path\nthrough EX to the fetch PC and an EX ALU path. The execute datapath\nneeds a shorter divide recurrence and fabric-registered operands to\nconvert that improvement into a faster core clock.\n\nhyp-20261122-002-r7s1\nBuffer decoded instructions ahead of register read and issue\nThe bench champion scores 201.60 CoreMark iterations/s at a median\n85.341 MHz and 4,233,123 marker cycles. Its combinational IF/ID path\naccepts a fetch only when decode can issue it immediately. A load-use\ninterlock or dmem stall wastes a ready imem response, and an imem stall\ncan leave EX idle after the back end becomes ready. Earlier fetch\nqueues reduced marker cycles, but the round-six raw-packet FIFO with\nregistered recovery reached 76.709 MHz on its parent. Decoding before\nthe buffer puts opcode validation and immediate generation in parallel\nwith the front end's target generation. On a buffered issue, the\ndecoded fields come directly from storage while the source tags drive\nregister reads and forwarding checks.\n\nhyp-20261122-002-r8s1\nRegister fetch address candidates before steering\nThe bench champion scores 216.99 iterations/s at a median 86.362 MHz over\n3,979,945 CoreMark marker cycles. Its reported 16.665 ns Gowin path starts\nat the synthetic instruction source and ends at the fetch request register.\nThe direct target goes through target arithmetic, the aperture check, and\nnext-PC selection before it reaches that register. A scratch implementation\nwith separate full-width registers for all four address candidates preserved\nthe marker count and reached 87.023 MHz median. Its critical path shifted\nto the divider. Scratch variants that merged replay with the sequential\nlane or retimed the FIFO squash scored lower. Keep the four distinct lanes\nand reduce the speculative target lane to the address bits it can use.\n\n-rwxrwx---+ 1 hwebench hwebench 243880 Nov 22 09:45 /srv/hwebench/tmp/7c172beb/a589e53d/bench-structural.uNuQOA/obj/cosim_sim\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
