{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_72", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'nl -ba cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r10s2.yaml'", "aggregated_output": "     1\tid: hyp-20261122-003-r10s2\n     2\ttitle: \"Read predicted loop words one cycle ahead of replay\"\n     3\tcategory: predictor\n     4\tmotivation: |\n     5\t  The champion runs ten stalled CoreMark iterations in 3,979,945 cycles at\n     6\t  86.362 MHz. An earlier trace counted 65,243 redirects, so improving branch\n     7\t  direction alone has limited headroom. The r9s2 sequential loop replay\n     8\t  prototype reached 3,713,902 cycles and 85.359 MHz in scratch measurements.\n     9\t  Its tournament formal run timed out. Replay can retain most of those cycle\n    10\t  savings while keeping replay lookup and fence state off the ready-bus\n    11\t  issue and recovery paths.\n    12\thypothesis: |\n    13\t  Train a loop stream predictor on advancing legal conditional backedges\n    14\t  with aligned endpoints inside the 1 MiB instruction aperture and spans\n    15\t  of at most 64 words. Register the EX observation before qualifying the\n    16\t  interval. Fill a 64-entry tagged table from accepted ready words in that\n    17\t  interval. Store the raw instruction, full remaining word-address tag and\n    18\t  validity. Fill only sequential instructions, excluding conditional\n    19\t  branches, jumps and FENCE.I. Changing the interval leaves unrelated\n    20\t  tagged entries resident.\n    21\t\n    22\t  Split the table into two 32-entry banks by PC[2]. Every cycle read the\n    23\t  effective request PC and PC+4. Address each bank by PC[7:3] for its\n    24\t  lookup, advancing the even-bank row on an odd request. Form the\n    25\t  even-bank index increment and its upper tag adjustment in parallel.\n    26\t  Compare each returned PC[19:8] tag within the aperture and register\n    27\t  the word and hit bit. On the next cycle, when the request held or\n    28\t  advanced sequentially, its parity selects the registered candidate.\n    29\t  Mask the old candidates for one cycle after an accepted taken\n    30\t  prediction or a registered EX redirect. Read the new pair in that\n    31\t  cycle so a stalled request can replay on the following cycle\n…[1959 of 5031 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5cbd385531ef6c7a]…\nO pressure, stalled recovery, speculative\n    60\t  fence squash and code replacement across FENCE.I.\n    61\texpected_impact:\n    62\t  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n    63\t  confidence: medium\n    64\tchanges:\n    65\t  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    66\t    description: \"Add the banked loop predictor, parallel current and successor lookups, and registered replay lane. Decouple physical FIFO writes from tail acceptance and qualify the aperture hold with registered recovery.\"\n    67\t  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    68\t    description: \"Export the branch PC and exact direct target alongside the existing branch advance and direction signals. Export an advancing FENCE.I pulse.\"\n    69\t  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    70\t    description: \"Connect the backedge and fence observations to fetch while preserving the single-channel interface.\"\n    71\t  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    72\t    description: \"Add replay tests for consecutive stalled beats, bank and tag boundaries, FIFO pressure, redirects, fence invalidation and retirement order.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
