{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_39", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261122-002-r9s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; keys=(\\\"id\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\"); [print(json.dumps({k:r.get(k) for k in keys},indent=2)) for l in sys.stdin if (r:=json.loads(l))[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"hyp-20261122-002-r9s1\\\"]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261122-002-r9s1\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The champion scores 216.99 iterations/s at 86.362 MHz over 3,979,945\\nmarker cycles. The four-entry queue hides short imem stalls while it has\\nwork. On an empty queue it waits for imem even when the requested word\\nalready passed through issue. Round eight's separate loop replay buffer\\nsaved 5.64% of cycles at 80.894 MHz. A shared decoded-packet store can\\nretain fall-through words across issue and serve both first-time and\\nrepeated fetches through one registered queue head.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Use 32 direct-mapped slots indexed by the word PC to hold decoded issue\\npackets, with exact remaining PC tags and separate reuse-valid bits.\\nKeep four FIFO reference entries. A live accepted word writes its\\ndecoded packet into the indexed slot and queues that slot number. A\\nreferenced slot is pinned until its last outstanding reference drains.\\nOn a ready response that aliases a pinned slot, hold the request and\\nlet the FIFO drain in order. On an imem stall, accept a stored packet\\nonly on an exact valid tag match. Limit reuse to fall-through words\\naway from the last word of the instruction aperture, so reuse advances\\nby PC+4 and conditional and indirect transfers still use live fetch.\\n\\nRegister the oldest queued payload at the issue boundary. Read the\\nsecond reference ahead of a possible pop and replace the head on the\\npop edge. When a new arrival becomes the head, take the live decoded\\nresponse or the payload at the request slot. Preserve empty-queue\\nflow-through for a ready live response and register a reused packet\\nbefore issue. Keep the two five-bit source tags with each reference\\nand the registered head so the hazard and register-file read paths\\nstart from fabric flops. Keep a narrow indexed copy for reused source\\ntags and advance it with the same acceptance as the payload.\\n\\nTrack the four reference-valid bits separately from packet reuse\\nvalidity. Use the registered redirect to make old references\\nimmediately invisible\n…[4315 of 7387 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:974df1052d9c674a]…\n 1, and 2 were 76.008, 81.083, and 81.083 MHz. The 81.083 MHz median yields 218.11 iterations/s and falls short of the 84.38 MHz promotion threshold. The slower placement was limited by fetch prediction to the next request and slot lookup to reference validity. The other two placements were limited by EX recovery to the slot register, with the divider close behind.\\n- The immediate/target field reduced the area of the packet RAM and head. A further split of the fetch target adder preserved the marker count and lowered the measured frequency, so the submitted RTL keeps the original target adder. Bitwuzla confirmed equality and signed and unsigned ordering for the submitted byte comparator over all 32-bit operands.\\n- The local single-channel formal run was incomplete within the implementation window. Six of 53 checks finished and passed, including liveness, uniqueness, illegal-instruction trapping, cover, causal ordering, and backward PC consistency. No counterexample was reported before the run stopped.\\n\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
