{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_61","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261122-003-r7s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"].get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"\\\")) for l in sys.stdin if (r:=json.loads(l))[\\\"id\\\"]==\\\"hyp-20261122-003-r7s2\\\"]'\"","aggregated_output":"Run the champion's 64-entry gshare and direct JAL predictor at a request\nPC that can advance independently of decode. Put four flow-through entries\nbetween prediction and decode. Each queued packet carries its instruction,\nsource word PC, exact direct target, applied direction, and lookup index.\nFor a source in the 1 MiB fetch aperture, store only PC[19:2]. Even a\nsigned JAL displacement leaves the full direct target between -1 MiB and\n2 MiB, exclusive of the upper bound. Store target[20:2] and target[31].\nExpand the target as {{11{target[31]}}, target[20:2], bit1, 1'b0}, deriving\nbit1 from the stored instruction (bit 21 for JAL, bit 8 otherwise).\nStore the two low bits of the lookup index because its upper four bits\nare PC[7:4]. Reconstruct the full index from the packet's own PC bits and\nsaved index bits. The resulting payload is 73 bits and needs no target\nadder on dequeue. Carry the full-width direct target on empty bypass,\nincluding requests outside the aperture.\n\nUse a packed asynchronous-read, synchronous-write distributed RAM with\nwrap-bit head and tail pointers. Write into a free tail based on registered\nspace. Advance the logical tail only when a ready response enters the\nqueue. A ready response with space can advance the request PC whether it\nbypasses or enqueues. Dequeue the oldest response on decode acceptance,\neven when imem is stalled. A full queue resumes fetching after a pop. Let\nthe last aperture word issue through empty bypass only. If it predicts\nfall-through, wait for EX before exposing the successor, and suppress\nduplicate issue while waiting. Requests outside the aperture also use\nempty bypass and follow the existing full-width PC semantics.\n\nKeep the previously measured one-bubble registered recovery scheme.\nCapture the alternate address each cycle, using PC+4 for a predicted-taken\ndirect transfer, the saved target for a predicted fall-through direct\ntransfer, and the forwarded JALR target for JALR. Register the miss bit\nseparately on EX handoff. A separate registered resume bit selects\n0x00100000 on a resolved sequential successor from a deferred last-word\nfetch. Recovery selects the next request and invalidates the younger\nID/EX instruction and queued packets. Let a ready recovery response\nbypass straight to ID, and retain its full address for retry if the\nresponse cannot issue. Keep the actual successor and alignment traps in\nEX for RVFI. Train exactly once on each advancing legal conditional\nbranch using its saved lookup index and resolved comparison, including\nwhen the taken target traps on alignment. Preserve the champion's banked\nregister file, one-hot forwarding, split dmem address path, and nine-edge\ndivider schedule.\n\nAt 3,979,945 marker cycles, the acceptance hurdle of 210.8736 iter/s\nrequires about 83.93 MHz median in Gowin. Matching the champion's clock\nwould give approximately 214.43 iter/s, a 6.36% gain. Confidence is low\nbecause the compact queue has yet to be placed with the champion backend.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
