{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor line in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n d=json.loads(line)\n if d['id'].endswith(('r8s2','r9s2','r10s2','r11s2','r12s2','r13s2','r13s0')):\n  print(d['id'], list(d)); print(d['hypothesis']); print(str(d.get('implementation_notes',''))[:5200])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-003-r8s2 ['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\n{'motivation': 'The champion spends 3,979,945 cycles in the stalled CoreMark window.\\nA scratch trace found 65,243 redirects and more than 208,000 taken\\nconditional backedges spanning at most 16 words. A short-loop stream\\npredictor can use the gaps in imem readiness to keep feeding issue\\nwhile the current request sequence stays inside a trained loop.\\nA first replay prototype ran in 3,755,433 cycles with the canonical\\nCRCs, a 5.64% cycle reduction. Its 65.437 MHz Gowin median exposed a\\nserial replay lookup and request-PC mux that needs to be retimed.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Train one 16-word loop stream buffer from advancing, legal conditional\\nbranches that resolve taken to a lower, word-aligned PC, with both\\nPCs in the fetch aperture. Register the EX observation before checking\\nthe span. Keep the loop start and backedge as the descriptor. Clear\\nthe word-valid state when replacing it. Populate members from accepted\\nready responses and retain the decoded instruction and exact direct target. Index by\\nthe low four word-address bits. A loop can span two adjacent 16-word\\nblocks. Compare their upper address tags and use block-specific valid\\nbits so two PCs with the same index cannot be mistaken for one another.\\n\\nPrefer the live response on every ready cycle. During an imem stall,\\nreplay one valid member at the effective request PC if the issue FIFO\\ncan accept it. Recompute the applied direction and saved index using\\nthe current gshare state. A replayed branch resolves and trains through\\nthe normal EX path. A wrong successor on loop exit or another transfer\\nsquashes younger packets and immediate\n…[39128 of 42200 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:499ab2dcfde9187d]…\n younger stores, FENCE.I advance and squash, and final-aperture-word recovery. A separate combinational SAT check passed for the address and aperture arithmetic.\n- CoreMark passed the canonical CRCs in 3,650,945 stalled marker cycles, down 5.61% from 3,868,036. The ready-bus CoreMark run matched the baseline's entire RVFI trace, including retirement cycles and both marker positions.\n- The retained RTL keeps the split direct-target sum and the original recovery select logic. Its Gowin trial measured 82.802, 84.340, and 84.340 MHz with 4,829 logic cells. An alternate direct-target adder and recovery select reached 81.700 MHz median. The retained median yields 231.01 CoreMark iterations/sec, below the 250.19 baseline, with forwarding into the EX ALU limiting the median placements.\n- Local `formal/run_all.sh` did not finish within the implementation budget. It generated 53 checks. The completed PC backward, uniqueness, liveness, causality, and cover checks passed. No counterexample had been reported at handoff.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
