e go idle.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"\n13:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-003-r4s2\", \"title\": \"Run gshare ahead with a four-entry LUT-RAM fetch queue\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"EX redirects accounted for only about 63,000 cycles in the earlier gshare\\nprofile. The current champion executes ten iterations in 4,233,123 cycles\\nat 54.869 MHz, so direction accuracy alone has limited headroom. The prior\\ntwo-entry predictor runahea\n…[4998 of 8070 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:50c2f8dbd446db1f]…\nls of at most 16 words. A short loop can issue from FIFO\\nslots it already occupies. The 16-word physical depth fits\n43:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261122-003-r14s2\", \"title\": \"Queue references to branch-trained instruction streams\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion takes 3,868,036 stalled CoreMark marker cycles.\\nEarlier loop replay reached 3,549,156 cycles, but copying replay\\npackets through the issue FIFO cost enough Gowin Fmax to erase the\\ngain. A predictor that retains several hot branch paths in block RAM\\ncan cover stalls across loop boundaries. Queueing a slot number lets\\neach replayed instruction use its existing payload.\\n\", \"hypothes\ntotal 16\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 22 21:07 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 22 21:07 ..\n.agents:\ntotal 8\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench hwebench   40 Nov 22 21:07 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody   nogroup  4096 Nov 22 21:07 ..\n\n.codex:\ntotal 8\ndr-xr-xr-x   2 hwebench hwebench   40 Nov 22 21:07 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 12 nobody   nogroup  4096 Nov 22 21:07 ..\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
