dent payload\n  reads driven by slot references. Feed the added read port from the\n  saved 18-bit direct target in the staged source metadata for the\n  current PC. Read speculatively from a replicated synchronous metadata\n  table using the slot index. Carry the source hit, target, and collision\n  status across the read edge. The lookup address uses saved metadata\n  even if the source will issue sequentially, the bus\n…[2121 of 5193 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fb2c5b06aa689419]…\nf_stage.sv\n    description: \"Implement branch-trained reference replay with a parallel registered taken-target metadata lookup. Keep live bypass and FIFO payload writes independent of the added read lane, and publish target hits through the existing resident reference path.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Pass advancing EX and older late-MEM taken branch observations to the fetch predictor for admission training, using the existing recovery priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Export the qualified early branch source and resolved direct target for predictor admission and the advancing fence indication for replay invalidation accounting.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Export the qualified taken late-branch source and direct target for the older admission observation.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Exercise a stall on a predicted taken target, exact tag conflicts, coincident fills, older MEM recovery, and FENCE.I while target metadata is in flight.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
