{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'git diff --stat; git status --short --ignored=matching cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/; cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261122-003-r3s2.yaml'","aggregated_output":"!! cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/\nid: hyp-20261122-003-r3s2\ntitle: \"Run the branch predictor ahead of decode with a two-entry fetch queue\"\ncategory: predictor\nmotivation: |\n  In the champion's canonical CoreMark window, EX redirected 63,126 times.\n  The 4.6% fitness hurdle at the champion's clock calls for saving about\n  185,000 cycles. Today the predictor also stops whenever decode stops.\n  Keeping prediction and fetch active across load-use, divide and dmem\n  holds lets the core use ready imem cycles that would otherwise go idle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Let the existing fetch-time gshare/JAL predictor steer the imem request\n  PC ahead of decode through a two-entry flow-through FIFO. On each ready\n  response with space, advance the request PC to its predicted successor\n  and accept the complete IF/ID packet, including its own PC, instruction,\n  direct target, applied direction and gshare index. Bypass the FIFO\n  when empty and decode can accept. Pop the oldest packet when decode can\n  accept even if imem is stalled. Allow concurrent pop and refill when full,\n  and otherwise hold the request PC when a full FIFO cannot accept.\n\n  Make EX redirect override request-PC hold and clear the queue and ID/EX\n  regardless of imem readiness. A load-use bubble holds the queue head for\n  retry and leaves queued predictions intact. Keep the dmem hold priority\n  so a blocked EX instruction neither redirects nor trains until advance.\n  Preserve the resolved-history update and queued counter update using\n  each EX branch's saved lookup index. Prediction metadata travels with the\n  instruction and EX continues to report the resolved successor to RVFI.\n\n  A scratch two-entry circular FIFO prototype passed the canonical CRCs\n  with both bus stalls and reduced bracketed cycles from 4,198,541 to\n  3,984,611. Gowin placement options reported 46.456, 48.860 and 48.860 MHz,\n  giving 122.62 iter/sec versus 116.81 for the champion. At that cycle\n  count the candidate needs a median above 48.68 MHz to qualify. Check\n  the median again after implementation because the margin is small.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 5\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add the two-entry circular FIFO with an empty bypass. Run gshare and direct target prediction at the independently advancing request PC. Accept, buffer and dequeue complete prediction packets, and clear occupancy on reset and redirect.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Make the frontend consume decision follow ID/EX acceptance. Let IF handle imem readiness locally while preserving load-use bubble insertion and dmem and divide holds.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect the decode hold to the FIFO consumer and pass imem readiness to fetch. Keep the EX recovery connection for both ID/EX squash and queued wrong-path discard.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check queue fill while decode is held, ordered drain through imem backpressure, and wrong-path packet and store discard after a held mispredict. Preserve the exact zero-wait divider and load-use gap checks.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
