{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -- '--istall|--dstall|--json|--quiet|--uart|--no-trace|marker_cycles' test/cosim/main.cpp tools/eval/fpga.py; cat cores/bench/test/_helpers.py; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"tools/eval/fpga.py:77:COREMARK_SIM_FLAGS = [\"--bench\", \"--istall\", \"--dstall\"]\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:63:        std::cerr << \"usage: sim <elf> [maxcycles] [--bench] [--istall] [--dstall] [--seed N]\\n\";\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:68:    // --istall: random ~22% imem-bus backpressure (VexRiscv-style).\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:69:    // --dstall: same on dmem bus. The orchestrator's fitness eval\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:78:        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--istall\") == 0) istall     = true;\ntest/cosim/main.cpp:79:        else if (std::strcmp(argv[i], \"--dstall\") == 0) dstall     = true;\n\"\"\"Shared cocotb constants and runner helpers for unit tests.\n\nConstants mirror rtl/core_pkg.sv. If a localparam there changes, change\nthe matching value here.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# cocotb 2.x moved the runner from cocotb.runner to cocotb_tools.runner.\nfrom cocotb_tools.runner import get_runner\n\n# ── ALU encodings (rtl/core_pkg.sv) ────────────────────────────────────────\nALU_ADD    = 0\nALU_SUB    = 1\nALU_AND    = 2\nALU_OR     = 3\nALU_XOR    = 4\nALU_SLT    = 5\nALU_SLTU   = 6\nALU_SLL    = 7\nALU_SRL    = 8\nALU_SRA    = 9\nALU_LUI    = 10\nALU_MUL    = 11\nALU_MULH   = 12\nALU_MULHU  = 13\nALU_MULHSU = 14\nALU_DIV    = 15\nALU_DIVU   = 16\nALU_REM    = 17\nALU_REMU   = 18\n\n# ── BranchOp encodings (= funct3 of BRANCH opcode) ─────────────────────────\nBR_BEQ  = 0\nBR_BNE  = 1\nBR_BLT  = 4\nBR_BGE  = 5\nBR_BLTU = 6\nBR_BGEU = 7\n\n# ── Paths ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nREPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nRTL       = REPO_ROOT / \"rtl\"\nTEST_DIR  = REPO_ROOT / \"test\"\nSIM_BUILD = REPO_ROOT / \"sim_build\"\n\n\ndef run_cocotb(toplevel: str, sources: list[str], test_module: str) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Build the DUT under Verilator and run the given cocotb test_module.\n\n    `sources` is a list of bare filenames under rtl/. Order matters —\n    package files (e.g. core_pkg.sv) come first.\n    \"\"\"\n    sim = os.environ.get(\"SIM\", \"verilator\")\n    runner = get_runner(sim)\n    build_dir = SIM_BUILD / toplevel\n\n    runner.build(\n        sources=[str(RTL / s) for s in sources],\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n        always=True,\n        build_args=[\"-Wall\", \"-Wno-fatal\", \"-Wno-style\"],\n    )\n    runner.test(\n        hdl_toplevel=toplevel,\n        test_module=test_module,\n        test_dir=str(TEST_DIR),\n        build_dir=str(build_dir),\n    )\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'trial_dir=\"$TMPDIR/r8s2-predictor/variants.bSVQ0x\"\nPREDICTOR_VARIANTS=\"$trial_dir\" PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -u - <<'\"'PY'\nimport concurrent.futures\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build\n\nroot = Path.cwd()\noriginal = root / 'cores/bench/rtl'\nscratch = Path(os.environ['PREDICTOR_VARIANTS'])\ncombined = (scratch/'parallel/if_stage.sv').read_text()\nplain = (original/'if_stage.sv').read_text()\nsplit_start, split_end = '  logic [11:0] upper_pc', '  assign direct_bit1'\nfor name in ('parallel-only', 'split-only'):\n    shutil.copytree(original, scratch/name, copy_function=shutil.copyfile)\n    if name == 'parallel-only':\n        src = combined[:combined.index(split_start)] + plain[plain.index('  assign direct_word'):plain.index(split_end)] + combined[combined.index(split_end):]\n        src = src.replace('direct_in_aperture', \\\"direct_word[31:20] == 12'b0\\\")\n    else:\n        src = plain[:plain.index('  assign direct_word')] + combined[combined.index(split_start):combined.index(split_end)] + plain[plain.index(split_end):]\n        src = src.replace(\\\"direct_word[31:20] == 12'b0\\\", 'direct_in_aperture')\n    (scratch/name/'if_stage.sv').write_text(src)\nwith concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=6) as pool:\n    builds = {pool.submit(build, root, scratch/name, 'fpga/core_bench_si.sv', option, scratch/f'{name}-{option}'): (name, option)\n              for name in ('parallel', 'parallel-only', 'split-only') for option in range(3)}\n    for future in concurrent.futures.as_completed(builds):\n        result = future.result()\n        print(builds[future], result.get('fmax_mhz'), result.get('reason'), (result.get('critical_paths') or [None])[0], flush=True)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'clock|STALL|GOWIN|GOWIN_HOME' fpga/constraints/clock.sdc; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x = json.loads(l)\n if x['category'] == 'predictor':\n  print(x['id'], x.get('cycles'), x.get('seeds'), x.get('fitness'))\n  if x['id'].endswith(('r2s2','r3s2')):\n   print(x.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_21", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'clock|STALL|GOWIN|GOWIN_HOME' fpga/constraints/clock.sdc; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfor l in open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl'):\n x = json.loads(l)\n if x['category'] == 'predictor':\n  print(x['id'], x.get('cycles'), x.get('seeds'), x.get('fitness'))\n  if x['id'].endswith(('r2s2','r3s2')):\n   print(x.get('implementation_notes'))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "4:create_clock -name clock -period 5 [get_ports {clock}]\nhyp-20261122-003-r1s2 4234052 [4.908, 5.334, 5.334] 12.6\nhyp-20261122-003-r2s2 4198541 [45.723, 49.042, 49.042] 116.81\n# Bench gshare predictor\n\nIF predecodes legal conditional branches and JAL, computes their full RV32 direct targets with a 30-bit word-address adder, and carries immediate bit 1 separately for alignment. ID/EX captures the target, applied direction, and six-bit lookup index. For aligned targets within the 1 MiB instruction aperture, fetch predicts JAL taken and uses a 64-entry table of two-bit saturating counters for conditional branches.\n\nEX resolves direct transfers from the latched target and computes JALR from forwarded rs1 and the immediate. The resolved direction drives recovery, and the resolved successor feeds RVFI. A data-memory hold defers recovery and training. When EX advances, a redirect squashes ID/EX and takes priority over instruction-memory backpressure.\n\nEach advancing, opcode-legal conditional branch shifts its comparison outcome into the two-bit history, including when a taken misaligned target traps. A queued update uses the latched lookup index and reads the current counter on the following clock so consecutive updates to an alias accumulate.\n\nI flattened the EX result mux into mutually exclusive ALU, divide, and link result paths after the initial Gowin median measured 43.967 MHz. The final critical paths still run through the EX ALU to the EX/MEM register or dmem RAM. The final build used 3,416 logic cells and 765 registers.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 fast single-issue checks on both runs.\n- All 78 cocotb cases passed. Directed tests cover consecutive counter aliasing, reversals in both directions, stalled recovery, misaligned and reserved direct transfers, forwarded JALR, and the exact nine-cycle cold BEQ and eight-cycle predicted JAL divider retirement gaps.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed all five ELFs. The trace ELFs passed \n…[2402 of 5474 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:84f4769ed118f08a]…\n- `make bench` and `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed. Selftest and three random programs passed full RVFI trace comparison with both buses ready and with both stall generators enabled. Stalled CoreMark passed the canonical CRC and completion checks.\n- Gowin timing across placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 48.531, 49.349, and 49.349 MHz. `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` reproduced the 49.349 MHz median and measured 3,984,611 bracketed CoreMark cycles. The score was 123.85 iterations/s, 6.03% above the champion's 116.81 iterations/s and above the 4.6% hurdle.\n\nThe limiting setup paths run from the register file through EX forwarding and the ALU to data RAM. The median has about 0.66 MHz of margin over the qualification frequency at the measured cycle count.\n\nhyp-20261122-003-r4s2 3979945 [55.382, 57.942, 57.942] 145.58\nhyp-20261122-003-r5s2 3979945 [61.096, 64.667, 64.667] 162.48\nhyp-20261122-003-r6s2 3979945 [77.565, 76.709, 76.709] 192.74\nhyp-20261122-003-r7s2 3979945 [76.603, 84.192, 84.192] 211.54\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
