hrough the ALU. The predictor can\\nimprove cycles per iteration while keeping its lookup local to fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core fetches sequentially and discards one fetch slot whenever\\nEX redirects a taken branch or jump. There is no IF/ID register, so a\\ncorrect fetch-stage prediction can remove that entire bubble. The baseline\\ntiming report puts the longest path through the ALU. The predictor can\\nimprove cycles per iteration while keeping its lookup local to fetch.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Add a 16-entry direct-mapped branch target buffer indexed by fetch PC[5:2].\\nUse PC[19:6] as \n…[27591 of 30663 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f72261ff359d3f3c]…\n retry, and the existing EX recovery address. Select\\nthe next request with registered steering so the replay tag checks,\\nreadiness, and direction do not drive a wide data mux before the\\ncandidate registers. Store replay eligibility for direct transfers\\nwith the decoded member to keep target range checks off the replay\\nlookup. Place the block tag checks in parallel with the indexed read.\\nPreserve the empty FIFO bypass and same-edge EX squash. At the measured\\nreplay cycle count, promotion requires a Gowin median above 85.238 MHz.\\nAt the champion's clock this would yield about 6% higher fitness. The\\nretimed design must recover most of the initial prototype's clock loss\\nto clear the promotion hurdle.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 6, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Add the backedge-trained decoded loop buffer, block-tag checks and parallel successor registers. Steer accepted replay through the existing FIFO with fresh prediction metadata and s\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
