{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,170p' formal/wrapper_si.sv; sed -n '1,130p' formal/checks_si.cfg; sed -n '1,170p' tools/agents/_hyp_parse.py; rg -n 'GW_SH|GOWIN|FPGA' Makefile tools/eval/gowin.py | head -40; ls /srv/hwebench/toolchain\"", "aggregated_output": "// riscv-formal wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. Same shape and\n// memory model as wrapper.sv, but instantiates `core` with only the\n// channel-0 RVFI port set — no `_1` ports. The single-issue path produces\n// only ch0 checks; checks_si.cfg sets `nret 1` so genchecks does not\n// emit any `_ch1` tasks (no PREUNSAT-as-pass tally needed). Selected by\n// the orchestrator when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n`include \"rvfi_macros.vh\"\n\nmodule rvfi_wrapper (\n    input clock,\n    input reset,\n    `RVFI_OUTPUTS\n);\n    // Solver picks any 32-bit instruction each cycle.\n    (* keep *) `rvformal_rand_reg [31:0] imem_data;\n\n    // 8 KiB dmem (2048 words).\n    reg [31:0] dmem [0:2047];\n\n    wire [31:0] imem_addr;\n    wire [31:0] dmem_addr;\n    wire [31:0] dmem_wdata;\n    wire [3:0]  dmem_wen;\n    wire        dmem_ren;\n\n    always @(posedge clock) begin\n        if (dmem_wen[0]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][7:0]   <= dmem_wdata[7:0];\n        if (dmem_wen[1]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][15:8]  <= dmem_wdata[15:8];\n        if (dmem_wen[2]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][23:16] <= dmem_wdata[23:16];\n        if (dmem_wen[3]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][31:24] <= dmem_wdata[31:24];\n    end\n\n    core uut (\n        .clock              (clock),\n        .reset              (reset),\n        .io_imemAddr        (imem_addr),\n        .io_imemData        (imem_data),\n        .io_imemReady       (1'b1),\n        .io_dmemAddr        (dmem_addr),\n        .io_dmemWData       (dmem_wdata),\n        .io_dmemRData       (dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]]),\n        .io_dmemWEn         (dmem_wen),\n        .io_dmemREn         (dmem_ren),\n        .io_dmemReady       (1'b1),\n        // Channel 0 — the only retirement channel. With nret=1 in\n        // checks_si.cfg, every rvfi_* signal here is sized for a single\n        // channel, so the core's `_0` ports connect directly without\n        // slicing. No `_1` ports exist on the core's IO under nret=1.\n        .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid),\n        .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order),\n        .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn),\n\n…[3903 of 6975 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:84e6a8a5ff24e193]…\np(0)\n        else:\n            # Marker present but no valid id token follows: fail loudly\n            return None\n    # Marker absent: fall back to leftmost search\n    m = _HYP_ID.search(prompt)\n    return m.group(0) if m else None\nMakefile:82:\t@echo \"  make fpga TARGET=v1     — FPGA fitness eval (Gowin Fmax + CoreMark cycles)\"\nMakefile:135:# FPGA timing and area come from the vendor flow, Gowin EDA\ntools/eval/gowin.py:1:\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\ntools/eval/gowin.py:3:V2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\ntools/eval/gowin.py:22:GOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\ntools/eval/gowin.py:23:GOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\ntools/eval/gowin.py:35:    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\ntools/eval/gowin.py:133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\nbin\noss-cad-suite\nxpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'r7s1|r8s0|r8s1|r8s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; rows=[json.loads(s) for s in sys.stdin]; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"fitness\\\"],r[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"],r[\\\"cycles\\\"],r[\\\"critical_path\\\"],r[\\\"seeds\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",r[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"]) for r in rows if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r8s2\\\",\\\"r8s1\\\",\\\"r8s0\\\",\\\"r7s1\\\"))]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'r7s1|r8s0|r8s1|r8s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; rows=[json.loads(s) for s in sys.stdin]; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"fitness\\\"],r[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"],r[\\\"cycles\\\"],r[\\\"critical_path\\\"],r[\\\"seeds\\\"],\\\"\\\\n\\\",r[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"]) for r in rows if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r8s2\\\",\\\"r8s1\\\",\\\"r8s0\\\",\\\"r7s1\\\"))]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261122-002-r7s1 216.99 86.362 3979945 {'from': 'lfsr_4_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/request_word_q_18_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.371, 'arrival_ns': 16.665, 'logic_cells': 34, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']} [87.942, 86.362, 86.362] \n # Decoded issue FIFO\n\nFetch now runs the existing decoder and immediate generator alongside target generation. A four-entry asynchronous-read FIFO stores the raw instruction, decoded control, full immediate, PC, and prediction metadata. Empty-queue bypass advances both wrap-bit pointers. A full queue reopens fetch on the cycle after a pop. ID reads the selected instruction's encoded register tags and captures data and forwarding selections when scheduling that packet. Load and multiply dependencies insert a bubble without removing the head, while an EX hold leaves ID/EX in place and permits fetch to fill available slots.\n\nThe advancing EX instruction supplies the redirect and preselects the opposite path from the saved prediction. The direct redirect clears the FIFO and ID/EX validity. Fetch captures the redirect pulse and alternate address in parallel so its output changes to the corrected request on that same edge, including during imem backpressure. If the corrected request stalls, fetch copies the address into its normal request register for retry.\n\nA sequential response accepted at `0x000ffffc` carries an aperture tag. Fetch holds that address and inhibits further acceptance until the tagged instruction advances in EX or an older instruction redirects. If the tagged instruction resolves sequentially, the request advances to its fall-through address.\n\nThe FIFO RAM and ID/EX payload may capture a ready younger packet on a redirect edge. The same edge clears both FIFO pointers and ID/EX validity, so the captured data is unreachable. This keeps the late EX redirect off the wide data enables.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- The placement options reached 87.942, 86.362, and 86.362 MHz. At 3,979,945 CoreMark marker cycles, the 86.362 MHz median yields 216.99 iterations/s, 7.64% above the champ\n…[7506 of 10578 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e27502c323115c14]…\ncover both endpoint block tags, FIFO backpressure, ready-response priority, descriptor replacement, loop exit, and FENCE.I advance and squash.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and the three random programs with and without memory stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed CRC validation in 3,755,433 marker cycles, 5.64% fewer than the champion's 3,979,945 cycles.\n- Gowin measured 74.696, 80.894, and 80.894 MHz across the three placement options. The median of 80.894 MHz fell short of the 85.238 MHz promotion target. The slowest paths reach the issue-valid register and the FIFO pointer resets through recovery and issue control.\n- The first formal invocation stopped in Yosys parsing at the loop RAM width declaration. Applying `$bits` to a declared signal, as the existing FIFO does, resolved the error. The full suite remained incomplete within the local time budget. The causal, cover, illegal-instruction, liveness, backward-PC, and unique-order checks passed. The run produced no counterexample in the completed checks.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
